l Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"Espiritu Santo day tour (Sep-May)","source":"https://www.goworldtravel.com/snorkeling-sea-lions-sea-of-cortez/","hook":"play with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","si":"expedition","blurb":"play with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","commission":"local operator + DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Espiritu Santo full-day island + snorkel","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"premier","bookable":"permitted day tour incl. CONANP bracelet","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","hook":"uninhabited UNESCO desert island — beaches, sea lions, snorkel","si":"expedition","blurb":"uninhabited UNESCO desert island — beaches, sea lions, snorkel","commission":"local operator + DMC"},{"name":"Playa Balandra day trip (El Hongo)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"transfer/tour or self-drive + CONANP bracelet","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Balandra,_Baja_California_Sur","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Mexico''s most photographed beach, shallow turquoise flats, protected","si":"tropical","blurb":"Mexico''s most photographed beach, shallow turquoise flats, protected","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC transfer + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Malecon + sunset sail","si_tag":"Tropical Islands","status":"live","tier":"premier","bookable":"catamaran/sail charter","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/swim-with-whale-sharks-la-paz/","hook":"La Paz''s waterfront promenade and calm-bay sunset cruises","si":"tropical","blurb":"La Paz''s waterfront promenade and calm-bay sunset cruises","commission":"charter operator + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Salvatierra wreck dive","si_tag":"Dive Globally / Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"dive-within-cert charter","source":"https://lapazdivers.com/la-paz-dive-sites/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"1976 ferry wreck at 18–20 m, thriving artificial reef, diveable near year-round","si":"Dive Globally / Ocean Adventures","blurb":"1976 ferry wreck at 18–20 m, thriving artificial reef, diveable near year-round","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"dive operator + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When and how can I swim with whale sharks in La Paz?","a":"October 1 to April 30, on a licensed half-day snorkel in the bay''s protected refuge zone — never scuba. Encounters are capped at 5 swimmers plus a certified guide per shark for 30 minutes, with no touching, to protect the juveniles that feed there.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / bucketlistbri.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is La Paz a good island and beach base?","a":"Yes — it is the launch port for the whole Sea-of-Cortez set: protected Balandra, Tecolote, the Malecón waterfront and boat trips to UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo. It''s the quiet, low-key alternative to the Los Cabos corridor two hours south.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What is there to dive around La Paz?","a":"The signature dive is the Salvatierra, a 1976 ferry wreck at 18–20 m that''s now a thriving artificial reef, diveable near year-round, plus the El Bajo seamount. La Paz has its own recompression chamber (confirm status at booking) and DAN emergency is +1-919-684-9111.","source":"lapazdivers.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Missing the season, not crime. Whale sharks are gone May–Sep, sea lions close Jun 1–Aug 31, both are snorkel-only (no touch, no scuba), and hurricane season runs Jun–Nov. Book the Oct–Apr window ahead and carry trip insurance for summer/fall.","source":"scubaboard.com / dossier Safety Card, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"La Paz Whale Sharks & Sea Lions: Sea of Cortez Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with whale sharks (Oct–Apr) and sea lions at Los Islotes, then sail to UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo — the quiet Baja capital on the Sea of Cortez. When and how to book.","slug":"la-paz-mexico","primary_keyword":"La Paz whale sharks","long_tail":["La Paz whale shark season 2026","swim with sea lions Los Islotes","Espiritu Santo tour from La Paz","Balandra beach La Paz guide","La Paz Sea of Cortez snorkel"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["tiburón ballena La Paz temporada","nadar con lobos marinos Los Islotes","tour Isla Espíritu Santo desde La Paz","Playa Balandra La Paz","snorkel Mar de Cortés La Paz","hoteles boutique La Paz Baja","buceo naufragio Salvatierra"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"Dive Globally / Ocean Adventures","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Baja Club","posture":"boutique-luxe, Design Hotels/Marriott (not full branded ultra)","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Marriott STARS/Design Hotels program","virtuoso_value_add":"amenity block (breakfast/credit/upgrade) where rate qualifies","mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.designhotels.com/hotels/mexico/baja-california-sur/la-paz/baja-club/"},{"name":"CostaBaja Resort & Spa (Puerta Cortes)","posture":"five-star resort (La Paz first five-star)","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application / host bedbank or preferred program","virtuoso_value_add":"amenity block where rate qualifies","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.costabajaresortspa.com/"},{"name":"Camp Cecil de la Isla (Espiritu Santo)","posture":"eco-luxe private-island glamping (8 tents, TOSEA)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or TOSEA operator terms","virtuoso_value_add":"private buy-out / naturalist upgrade on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"},{"name":"Puerta Cortes private beachfront villa (private pool/jacuzzi)","posture":"top private villa in gated marina-golf community","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application / villa-manager commission where offered; often OTA/Airbnb (affiliate)","virtuoso_value_add":"concierge + beach-club access","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/mx/beachfront-villa-private-pool-at-puerta-cortes.html"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"La Paz, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.1425,"lng":-110.3108}}'::jsonb, 55),
  ('lake-atitlan-guatemala', '10S', 'Lake Atitlán', 'Guatemala', '*If it''s the first pale light on three volcanoes', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Guatemala', '{"adventure","romance","culture","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Volcanic caldera lake at 1,562 m (5,125 ft), up to 340 m deep, ~130 km², ringed by three volcanoes — San Pedro, Tolimán, Atitlán (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Atitlán, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Villages divide by role: Panajachel gateway hub, San Pedro backpacker/Spanish-school, San Marcos yoga/wellness, Santiago Atitlán largest/traditional, San Juan weaving + coffee (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Indian Nose sunrise hike (~30 min pre-dawn) is the signature caldera overlook; San Marcos offers yoga retreats + Cerro Tzankujil cliff-jump (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Dry season Nov–Apr is most photogenic; Christmas + Semana Santa fill weeks ahead; Sept–Oct rates 40–50% below peak (Source: atitlan.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Air access via GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel; boat (lancha) is the only road between villages (Source: theabroadblog.com / adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police · 122/123 ambulance · 1500 ASISTUR/PROATUR (or +502-2290-2810) — verify locally","hospital":"Panajachel/Sololá clinics + regional hospital for stabilization; serious trauma/cardiac evac to Guatemala City (~3 hr road); highlands lack tertiary trauma capability","book_enabled":true,"state_dept_carveout":"US State Dept (reissued Jun 11 2026, codes C+T) explicitly names Lake Atitlán among destinations US-gov employees can visit; L4 zones = San Marcos Dept, Huehuetenango Dept, Zone 18 GC, Villa Nueva — none is Atitlán/Sololá","san_marcos_clarification":"L4 ''San Marcos Department'' (highland border dept) is a DIFFERENT place from ''San Marcos La Laguna,'' the safe yoga village on Lake Atitlán (Sololá)","l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on TWW''s BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) framing (same founder/attorney axis as the held Central-Mexico SR6)","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel","altitude":"~1,562 m (5,125 ft) lakeside — mild; volcano summits San Pedro ~3,020 m / Atitlán ~3,535 m reach real altitude","malaria":"none — CDC reports no malaria transmission at Lake Atitlán (highland); insect-bite precautions only; dengue/Zika possible in Guatemala generally","water":"bottled/purified only","lake_boat_safety":"Xocomil wind kicks up late morning/afternoon and can capsize boats — cross early, licensed lanchas with life vests","swim_advisory":"verify current cyanobacteria (Microcystis) advisory before selling lake-swim (blooms 2009, 2015)"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"Dry-season demand builds from late Sept / early Oct for the Nov–Apr window; retreat + honeymoon bookings run longer lead","peak":"Dry season Nov–Apr; sharpest spikes Christmas–New Year and Semana Santa; weekly Chichi-market micro-peak Thu/Sun","fire_date":"Mid-September for the Christmas/New-Year + Jan–Mar dry-season peak; early-to-mid January for the Semana Santa spike — curve-start minus 1–2 weeks (directional, sharpen on live tracking)","shoulder":"May–June and September–October","green":"May–October wet season — afternoon storms, greenest landscape, Sept–Oct rates 40–50% below peak","booking_lead":"Peak boutiques/villas 2–4 mo (longer for Christmas + Semana Santa); yoga retreats 2–6 mo; day tours day-of to 1 wk","off_season_specials":"Rainy-season wellness-retreat + language-immersion + villa packages; midweek boutique value; Chichi day-trip add-ons year-round","event_peaks":"Semana Santa (Mar/Apr), Christmas–New Year, Santiago Atitlán Maximón/Holy-Week processions"},"jewels":[{"name":"Indian Nose (Nariz del Indio) sunrise hike","si_tag":"Global / Epic Adventures","status":"live","hook":"~30-min pre-dawn ridge trek to a panoramic caldera + three-volcano overlook ''in perfect silence''","bookable_category":"guided sunrise hike + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","si":"Global / Epic Adventures","blurb":"~30-min pre-dawn ridge trek to a panoramic caldera + three-volcano overlook ''in perfect silence''","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"San Pedro / Atitlán volcano summit","si_tag":"Global / Epic Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided ascent of San Pedro (~3,020 m) or the harder Atitlán/Tolimán cones","bookable_category":"guided volcano trek","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Atitl%C3%A1n (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Global / Epic Adventures","blurb":"Guided ascent of San Pedro (~3,020 m) or the harder Atitlán/Tolimán cones","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP the caldera","si_tag":"Global / Epic Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Morning paddle across glass-calm water beneath the volcanoes; cleanest near San Marcos","bookable_category":"rental + guided paddle","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","si":"Global / Epic Adventures","blurb":"Morning paddle across glass-calm water beneath the volcanoes; cleanest near San Marcos","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Village-hop by lancha","si_tag":"Global / Epic Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Full-day boat circuit of the lakeside villages — each a distinct world","bookable_category":"private/shared lancha day","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Global / Epic Adventures","blurb":"Full-day boat circuit of the lakeside villages — each a distinct world","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC / boat operator","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Chichicastenango market (Thu & Sun)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Guatemala''s most famous Maya market — textiles, masks, Santo Tomás church, Pascual Abaj shrine","bookable_category":"guided day trip from Atitlán","tier":"comfort","source":"https://dmcfinder.com/listing/clark-tours/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Guatemala''s most famous Maya market — textiles, masks, Santo Tomás church, Pascual Abaj shrine","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC (Clark/Martsam) / activity affiliate (browsing = non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"San Juan La Laguna textile + natural-dye co-ops","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Women''s weaving cooperatives (e.g. Lema'') — backstrap looms + indigo/cochineal natural dyes","bookable_category":"co-op weaving demo + shop","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Women''s weaving cooperatives (e.g. Lema'') — backstrap looms + indigo/cochineal natural dyes","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Santiago Atitlán + Maximón","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The lake''s largest, most traditional Tz''utujil town + the Maximón folk-saint shrine (moved yearly among cofradías)","bookable_category":"guided cultural visit","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The lake''s largest, most traditional Tz''utujil town + the Maximón folk-saint shrine (moved yearly among cofradías)","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC / guide (shrine tip = non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"San Juan coffee cooperatives","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Farm-to-cup tours at highland coffee co-ops; small-lot Guatemalan coffee story","bookable_category":"coffee-farm tour + tasting","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Farm-to-cup tours at highland coffee co-ops; small-lot Guatemalan coffee story","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"San Marcos La Laguna yoga + retreats","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","hook":"Central America''s yoga village — Las Pirámides del Ká, Eagle''s Nest, retreat centers + vegetarian cafés","bookable_category":"retreat program + wellness stay","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"Central America''s yoga village — Las Pirámides del Ká, Eagle''s Nest, retreat centers + vegetarian cafés","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"retreat referral / hotel","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Cerro Tzankujil cliff-jump reserve (San Marcos)","si_tag":"Wellness","status":"future","hook":"Natural reserve with trails + lakeside cliff-jump platform — the lake''s famous swim spot","bookable_category":"reserve entry + guided add-on","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventurouskate.com/the-towns-of-lake-atitlan-guatemala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"Dry season Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wellness","blurb":"Natural reserve with trails + lakeside cliff-jump platform — the lake''s famous swim spot","when":"Dry season Nov–Apr","commission":"activity add-on (entry = non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Private-boat sunset + volcano golden hour","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Chartered lancha sunset cruise or private-dock dinner beneath the three volcanoes","bookable_category":"private-boat charter + dining","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.jacadatravel.com/latin-america/guatemala/lake-atitlan/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","si":"romance","blurb":"Chartered lancha sunset cruise or private-dock dinner beneath the three volcanoes","commission":"DMC / hotel F&B + villa","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the Indian Nose sunrise hike, and can you climb the volcanoes?","a":"The Indian Nose (Nariz del Indio) is a ~30-minute pre-dawn ridge trek to a panoramic caldera-and-three-volcano overlook \"in perfect silence\" — Atitlán''s signature dawn. You can also summit the harder volcanoes (San Pedro ~3,020 m, Atitlán ~3,535 m), which reach real altitude, so go guided-only.","source":"adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"global"},{"q":"Where do you stay for a honeymoon at Lake Atitlán?","a":"At the lake''s one true-luxury anchor: Casa Palopó, Guatemala''s only Relais & Châteaux hotel — a ~15-room boutique above Santa Catarina Palopó with three-volcano views. Beneath it sit eco-luxury Laguna Lodge and full-staff cliffside private villas with private docks, ideal for honeymoons and small buyouts.","source":"jacadatravel.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the Chichicastenango market?","a":"Thursdays and Sundays only. It''s Guatemala''s most famous Maya market — textiles, masks, produce, the Santo Tomás church and the hillside Pascual Abaj shrine — booked as a guided day-trip from Atitlán, because those are the two K''iche'' Maya trading days that drive the weekly highland micro-peak.","source":"dmcfinder.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Lake Atitlán good for a yoga retreat?","a":"Yes — San Marcos La Laguna is Central America''s best-known yoga village, with retreat centers like Las Pirámides del Ká and Eagle''s Nest plus a cluster of vegetarian cafés and a genuine decades-old community. Retreats run set calendars, so wellness bookings often carry a 2–6-month lead.","source":"adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on the lake?","a":"The wind, not the water quality. The Xocomil — a Pacific-vs-northern wind collision — kicks up late morning and afternoon and is \"capable of capsizing boats,\" so cross early on licensed lanchas with life vests. Separately, verify the current cyanobacteria (Microcystis) swim advisory before booking lake-swim.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Atitlán Travel Guide — Volcanoes, Maya Villages & Chichi Market | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The most beautiful lake in the world: three volcanoes, a dozen Maya villages, San Marcos yoga, San Juan weavers, Santiago''s Maximón, the Chichicastenango market, and Casa Palopó (Relais & Châteaux). Bookable with mandatory L3 disclosure.","slug":"lake-atitlan-guatemala","primary_keyword":"Lake Atitlán travel guide","long_tail":["best time to visit Lake Atitlán 2026","is Lake Atitlán safe 2026","Lake Atitlán villages guide","San Marcos La Laguna yoga retreat","Indian Nose sunrise hike","Chichicastenango market days","Casa Palopó Relais & Châteaux","San Juan La Laguna weaving cooperative","how to get to Lake Atitlán from Guatemala City"],"search_language":"es-GT","local_keywords":["Lago de Atitlán qué hacer","¿es seguro viajar al Lago de Atitlán?","mejores hoteles Lago de Atitlán","Chichicastenango mercado","nariz del indio caminata amanecer","San Marcos La Laguna yoga","San Juan La Laguna tejidos","cómo llegar al Lago de Atitlán desde Guatemala"],"hreflang":["en","es-GT"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"adventure","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Casa Palopó (Relais & Châteaux)","why_ultra":"Guatemala''s only Relais & Châteaux hotel — ~15 individually designed suites above Santa Catarina Palopó with three-volcano views; the lake''s benchmark true-luxury property","earning":"on application / Relais & Châteaux via Virtuoso/Fora","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Laguna Lodge Eco-Resort","why_ultra":"Premier eco-luxury boat-access boutique on a private lakeside reserve; sustainability-forward design + spa; the lake''s top eco-luxury play","earning":"on application / host program","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Cliffside private villas (Santa Cruz / Tzununá / San Marcos)","why_ultra":"Full-staff private lake houses with private docks + caldera terraces — the ultra-villa alternative for honeymoons + small buyouts","earning":"via specialist villa desk + MoR","mor":true,"tier":"luxury-ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Lake Atitlán, Guatemala"},"geo":{"lat":14.6907,"lng":-91.2025}}'::jsonb, 56),
  ('lake-titicaca-puno-peru', '10S', 'Lake Titicaca (Puno), Peru', 'Peru', 'Lake Titicaca (Puno)', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Lima, South Coast & Amazon', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"105","tourist_help":"iPerú (national tourist assistance line)","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"Juliaca (JUL) via Lima (LIM); or rail/road from Cusco & Arequipa","altitude_m":{"lake_titicaca_puno":3810,"taquile":3800,"amantani_temple_hills":4100},"altitude_rule":"Highest stop on most Peru circuits (higher than Cusco); arrive already acclimatized (ideally Arequipa→Colca→Puno→Cusco); gradual island climbs; coca/soroche management; consider Diamox","cold_nights":"Bitterly cold altiplano nights; island homestays unheated — pack layers","water":"bottled/purified only","remoteness_note":"Islands have basic facilities only; serious emergencies require boat to Puno then evac to Arequipa/Lima","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Within 20km south of the Peru-Colombia border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers ( VRAEM ) FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel to these two areas for safety and security reasons."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town This is due to a high level of violence from organised criminal gangs who produce and traffic illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"May–September (dry-season altiplano)","event_peak":"Virgen de la Candelaria — ~Jan 16 – Feb 10 (main day Feb 2, dance apex Feb 8–10); secondary Inti Raymi-season (late June) overflow","inflection_curve_start":"early December (Candelaria) / early April (dry-season core)","fire_date":"mid–late November (Candelaria/Feb) & mid–late March (May–Sep core)","green_offseason":"November–March (minus the February Candelaria spike)","binding_constraint":"Candelaria lodging sellout + acclimatization sequencing; often booked as the Cusco↔Arequipa overland link"},"jewels":[{"name":"Uros floating reed islands","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.theonlyperuguide.com/peru-guide/puno/uros-floating-islands/","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"hand-built totora-reed islands ~30 min by boat from Puno, springy underfoot, where the Uros people still live and build. Real communities","si":"culture","blurb":"hand-built totora-reed islands ~30 min by boat from Puno, springy underfoot, where the Uros people still live and build. Real communities","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC/operator day tour + Uros community landing fee (non-comm) + reed-craft retail"},{"name":"Taquile Island (UNESCO textile island)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/taquile-and-its-textile-art-00166","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"terraced island where knitting is done by men and weaving by women; the textile art is on UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list","si":"culture","blurb":"terraced island where knitting is done by men and weaving by women; the textile art is on UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC/operator day or 2-day tour + community entry (non-comm) + textile-cooperative retail"},{"name":"Amantaní homestay + starry night","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.peroudecouverte.com/peru-puno-amantani-island-homestay-pachamama-en.html","hook":"the deepest cultural time on the lake: overnight with a Quechua family, shared meals, dance in borrowed dress","si":"culture","blurb":"the deepest cultural time on the lake: overnight with a Quechua family, shared meals, dance in borrowed dress","commission":"direct-to-community co-op (thin margin) + homestay/community fee (non-comm)"},{"name":"Sillustani chullpa towers (sunset)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machutravelperu.com/blog/puno-sillustani","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"pre-Inca Colla funerary towers up to 12 m tall on a peninsula over Lake Umayo, ~35 km from Puno","si":"culture","blurb":"pre-Inca Colla funerary towers up to 12 m tall on a peninsula over Lake Umayo, ~35 km from Puno","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/operator afternoon excursion + site entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"Virgen de la Candelaria festival (February)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.urosexpeditions.com/travel-news/candelaria-festival-2026-official-schedule-dance-order","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the largest folk-festival gatherings in the Americas: thousands of dancers, \"traje de luces\" sequined costumes, brass bands","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the largest folk-festival gatherings in the Americas: thousands of dancers, \"traje de luces\" sequined costumes, brass bands","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC festival package (hotel + guiding + stadium seating); book by mid–late Nov"},{"name":"Llachón peninsula community tourism (Capachica)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://titicacatravel-ip.com/en/tour/lake-titicaca/homestay-tour-llachon-amantani-taquile-islands","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the mainland community-tourism heartland on the Capachica peninsula: experiential homestays, weaving, cooking and sailing with families, quieter than the islands","si":"culture","blurb":"the mainland community-tourism heartland on the Capachica peninsula: experiential homestays, weaving, cooking and sailing with families, quieter than the islands","when":"May–September","commission":"direct-to-community co-op + DMC add-on"},{"name":"Aymara / Quechua living culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sillustani","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the altiplano is a living Aymara–Quechua cultural landscape; language, dress, agriculture and belief are the deep story that ties every island and shore together","si":"culture","blurb":"the altiplano is a living Aymara–Quechua cultural landscape; language, dress, agriculture and belief are the deep story that ties every island and shore together","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC cultural interpretation woven through every tour"},{"name":"Luxury catamaran day-sail (Peru-side)","si_tag":"GEA / RHN","tier":"comfort","source":"https://titicaca.cruises/en/home/","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a private or shared catamaran across the open lake. Outdoor decks, Cordillera views, and — on some operators","si":"GEA / RHN","blurb":"a private or shared catamaran across the open lake. Outdoor decks, Cordillera views, and — on some operators","when":"May–September","commission":"lake-operator net/commissionable tour (Peru-side only); private charter highest margin"}],"faq":[{"q":"Are the Uros, Taquile and Amantaní islands worth it — and does my money reach the families?","a":"Yes, and this is the reason to come. Booked through the community co-op, an Amantaní overnight homestay costs roughly $10–15 per person including meals and rotates through ten host communities, so the income reaches families directly rather than mainland middlemen — the deepest cultural experience on the lake.","source":"peroudecouverte.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How hard is the island walking, and what should I plan for?","a":"Plan for altitude, not difficulty. Island hikes run ~3,800–4,100 m — Taquile is a steady 30–60 minute uphill from the dock, and Amantaní''s twin temple hills top near 4,100 m — so the real risk is AMS. Arrive already acclimatized, pace the climb, and carry water.","source":"bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Lake Titicaca good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, as a quiet luxe add-on to a Cusco/Machu Picchu core. The standout is Titilaka, an 18-suite all-inclusive Relais & Châteaux lodge on a private peninsula with lake-view suites, a private jetty and oxygen-quiet calm — sunrise over the water and private catamaran sailing.","source":"relaischateaux.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Altitude — full stop. At ~3,810 m the lake is the highest stop on most Peru circuits, higher than Cusco, so AMS (soroche) is the dominant safety fact and outranks crime by a wide margin. Best practice: reach the lake already acclimatized (Arequipa→Colca→Puno→Cusco).","source":"turismoliberty.pe, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the boat trip across the lake dangerous?","a":"Only if you cut corners on the operator. Titicaca is a huge, cold, high-altitude open lake where afternoon wind picks up fast; insist on a licensed lancha with life vests and prefer guided/operator boats over informal transport. Weather can turn quickly on the altiplano.","source":"titicaca.cruises, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Titicaca & Puno, Peru — Uros, Taquile & Amantaní Guide, Altitude Tips & Luxury Lodges | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["Lago Titicaca Uros","islas flotantes Puno","Taquile Amantaní tour","homestay isla Amantaní","chullpas de Sillustani","Virgen de la Candelaria Puno 2026","mal de altura Puno soroche","cómo llegar a Puno desde Cusco","catamarán Lago Titicaca"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"primary_keyword":"Lake Titicaca (Puno)"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Titilaka (Relais & Châteaux)","location":"Private peninsula near Puno","earning":"Relais & Châteaux / Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR + VIP amenities (upgrade, breakfast, early/late, 50-min massage for two)","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"GHL Hotel Lago Titicaca","location":"Esteves Island","earning":"agency + affiliate; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Casa Andina Premium Puno","location":"Puno lakeshore","earning":"agency + affiliate; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Private catamaran (Peru-side day charter)","location":"Open lake ex-Puno","earning":"lake-operator charter; agency-coordinated","mor":"operator","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Lake Titicaca (Puno), Peru, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-15.8402,"lng":-70.0219}}'::jsonb, 57),
  ('lima-peru', '10S', 'Lima', 'Peru', 'The world''s table, on the Pacific', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Lima, South Coast & Amazon', '{"romance","expedition","culinary","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Home to the World''s #1 restaurant 2025 (Maido, Nikkei) plus Central (former #1, Best of the Best), Kjolle #9, Merito #26, Mayta #39 - a global top-tier food capital.","Pre-Inca adobe pyramids inside the modern city (Huaca Pucllana, ~200-700 AD, in Miraflores) alongside the UNESCO colonial Centro Historico and the Convento de San Francisco catacombs.","Jorge Chavez (LIM) is South America''s newest mega-hub: new $2.4B Fraport/LAP terminal opened June 1, 2025 (3x size, up to 40M pax/yr, 46 gates, 2nd runway); the gateway to Cusco/MP, the Amazon, Titicaca and the south coast.","Cool Pacific-desert climate: warm sunny summer Dec-Apr; grey misty ''garua'' winter May-Nov (dry but overcast) - the driest window for Machu Picchu, which drives Lima''s derivative winter spike.","Bohemian Barranco (Puente de los Suspiros) and clifftop Miraflores (Malecon, Costa Verde paragliding) anchor the boutique-romance line; genuine global-flag ultra (Belmond, Relais & Chateaux, LHW, JW Marriott)."],"safety":{"emergency":"105 National Police (PNP) / 106 SAMU medical-ambulance / 116 Bomberos (fire); iPeru tourist assistance (01-574-8000, desks at LIM/Miraflores/Larcomar)","hospital":"Lima has Peru''s best private hospitals/clinics (Clinica Anglo Americana, Ricardo Palma, Clinica Internacional) for stabilization; serious trauma routes to US medical evacuation - carry evac-capable insurance","advisory_level":"L2","bin":"freely bookable (L2)","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":"none (L2 is standard-caution, below disclosure threshold)","l3_disclosure":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Jorge Chavez Intl (LIM), Callao - new Fraport/LAP terminal opened 2025-06-01; SA hub; LIM->Miraflores ~45-60 min via hotel/DMC transfer (not street taxi)","urban_crime_discipline":"stay in Miraflores/Barranco/San Isidro; registered radio-taxi or ride-hail app or hotel transfer only (never unmarked street taxi - express-kidnapping setup); beware distraction theft; in-bank ATMs only; don''t display valuables","state_of_emergency_note":"Lima/Callao late-2025 state of emergency raised police/military presence amid rising urban crime - does not change L2 bin; verify current status live","altitude":"Lima at sea level (no altitude issue; useful soft-landing before Cusco 3,400 m / Titicaca 3,800 m)","dengue":"low on cool Lima coast; higher on Amazon/northern extensions","malaria":"no malaria risk in Lima (highland/coastal capital); Amazon extensions do carry risk - CDC consult for those legs","water":"bottled/purified only (also underpins reputable-cebicheria raw-fish hygiene rule)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Within 20km south of the Peru-Colombia border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers ( VRAEM ) FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene, and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel to these two areas for safety and security reasons."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km south of the Putumayo River and the border between Peru and Colombia (Loreto region) except for: the Amazon River the area of the triple border with Brazil and Colombia from and including the towns of Caballococha in Peru up to the actual triple border at Santa Rosa de Yavari town This is due to a high level of violence from organised criminal gangs who produce and traffic illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro Rivers, also known as the VRAEM region."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_coastal_summer":"Dec-Apr - Lima''s own warm/sunny curve (beaches, nightlife, paragliding, surfing); highest crowds/prices","inflection_gateway_winter":"Jun-Aug - derivative spike as travelers bookend the driest Machu Picchu window through Lima","garua":"May-Nov grey misty sea-fog winter (dry but overcast); sell as culinary/culture bookend, not beach","fire_date":"coastal-summer curve: fire ~mid-November (curve-start -1-2 wks); MP-derivative winter curve: fire ~mid-May; practically, attach Lima nights to whenever the parent Cusco/MP campaign fires","booking_lead":"top tasting menus (Central/Maido/Kjolle) weeks ahead - reservation-first; city hotels 2-3 months for summer; Cusco/Amazon-attached bookends 3-6 months","shoulder":"Apr-May & Sep-Nov (better deals, workable weather)","off_season_specials":"grey-winter ''gastronomy bookend'': tasting-menu circuit, cebicheria lunches, Larco/Pachacamac/San Francisco heritage, cooking classes, pisco-sour masterclasses","event_peaks":["Fiestas Patrias late July (Independence, domestic peak)","Mistura-successor gastronomy festival (name/dates UNVERIFIED - confirm live)","Christmas/New Year (summer)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Central / Maido / Kjolle tasting menus","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"The world-ranked Lima fine-dining trinity - Maido (World''s #1 2025), Central (Best of the Best), Kjolle (#9); book weeks ahead, reservation-first.","bookable_category":"direct reservation or DMC culinary program","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.theworlds50best.com/stories/News/maido-lima-the-worlds-best-restaurant-2025.html","si":"culinary","blurb":"The world-ranked Lima fine-dining trinity - Maido (World''s #1 2025), Central (Best of the Best), Kjolle (#9); book weeks ahead, reservation-first.","commission":"DMC culinary-program AOR 10-15%; raw restaurant deposit pass-through"},{"name":"La Mar cebicheria (Gaston Acurio)","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Acurio''s flagship Miraflores cebicheria (est. 2005), Latin America''s 50 Best - the definitive lunch-only ceviche experience.","bookable_category":"direct / DMC food tour (lunch only)","tier":"premier","source":"http://limacitykings.com/la-mar-cebicheria-peruana/","si":"culinary","blurb":"Acurio''s flagship Miraflores cebicheria (est. 2005), Latin America''s 50 Best - the definitive lunch-only ceviche experience.","commission":"DMC food-program AOR / Viator affiliate 4-8%; walk-in pass-through"},{"name":"Pisco Sour at the Country Club English Bar","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"SUMMUM-award-winning Pisco Sour (2012/2013/2022 best bar in Lima) in the 1927 hotel''s traditional English Bar.","bookable_category":"walk-in / hotel guest","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_Club_Lima_Hotel","si":"culinary","blurb":"SUMMUM-award-winning Pisco Sour (2012/2013/2022 best bar in Lima) in the 1927 hotel''s traditional English Bar.","commission":"pairs with Country Club stay (hotel AOR); bar spend pass-through"},{"name":"Huaca Pucllana","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Pre-Inca (~200-700 AD) adobe pyramid in the heart of Miraflores, with an acclaimed on-site restaurant overlooking the floodlit ruin.","bookable_category":"site tour / restaurant","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g294316-d311722-Reviews-Huaca_Pucllana-Lima_Lima_Region.html","si":"culture","blurb":"Pre-Inca (~200-700 AD) adobe pyramid in the heart of Miraflores, with an acclaimed on-site restaurant overlooking the floodlit ruin.","commission":"DMC/affiliate on tour; site fee + restaurant pass-through"},{"name":"Convento de San Francisco catacombs","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"1540 Franciscan monastery in the UNESCO Centro Historico with catacombs holding tens of thousands of bones.","bookable_category":"guided city tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"culture","blurb":"1540 Franciscan monastery in the UNESCO Centro Historico with catacombs holding tens of thousands of bones.","commission":"DMC/affiliate 4-10%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Larco Museum (Museo Larco)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Pre-Columbian masterpiece collection in an 18th-c. mansion over a pyramid, with a famed garden restaurant; the ''Huacas & Larco by night'' tour is a classic.","bookable_category":"entry / night tour + dinner","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Lima/Huacas-and-Larco-Museum-by-Night-with-Dinner/d928-7465P4","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Pre-Columbian masterpiece collection in an 18th-c. mansion over a pyramid, with a famed garden restaurant; the ''Huacas & Larco by night'' tour is a classic.","when":"year-round","commission":"Viator night-tour affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Pachacamac archaeological complex","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Vast pre-Inca/Inca pilgrimage city (pyramids, temples, plazas) ~30 km south of Lima with an on-site museum; easy half-day.","bookable_category":"DMC/Viator day tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Vast pre-Inca/Inca pilgrimage city (pyramids, temples, plazas) ~30 km south of Lima with an on-site museum; easy half-day.","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC 10-12% / affiliate 4-8%; site entry pass-through"},{"name":"Callao Monumental street-art district","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Regenerated Callao port-district arts quarter - murals, galleries and design studios in old republican buildings; go with a vetted tour.","bookable_category":"guided art tour (zone awareness)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Regenerated Callao port-district arts quarter - murals, galleries and design studios in old republican buildings; go with a vetted tour.","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/affiliate 4-10%; confirm live tour product + safe corridor"},{"name":"Barranco + Puente de los Suspiros","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Bohemian seafront district - murals, galleries, the romance-legend Bridge of Sighs and sunset bars; Lima''s honeymoon base.","bookable_category":"self-guided within corridor / guided art walk","tier":"luxury","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"romance","blurb":"Bohemian seafront district - murals, galleries, the romance-legend Bridge of Sighs and sunset bars; Lima''s honeymoon base.","commission":"pairs with Hotel B/Barranco boutique stay (hotel AOR); walk affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Miraflores Malecon + Parque del Amor at sunset","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Clifftop coastal promenade above the Pacific with the mosaic ''Park of Love'' - the classic Lima romance postcard, free.","bookable_category":"free / paired with clifftop dinner","tier":"essential","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"romance","blurb":"Clifftop coastal promenade above the Pacific with the mosaic ''Park of Love'' - the classic Lima romance postcard, free.","commission":"bundled into commissionable romance program / dinner"},{"name":"Tandem paragliding off the Miraflores cliffs","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided tandem flight over the Costa Verde clifftops and Pacific from the ~80 m Miraflores launch - the signature Lima adventure.","bookable_category":"reputable tandem operator / Viator (guided-only)","tier":"premier","source":"https://pariwana-hostel.com/en/blog/2025/10/07/paragliding-in-lima-a-complete-guide-to-flying-over-the-costa-verde/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided tandem flight over the Costa Verde clifftops and Pacific from the ~80 m Miraflores launch - the signature Lima adventure.","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 10-12%"},{"name":"Costa Verde surf lesson","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided surf school on the Miraflores/Barranco beach breaks (Makaha/Waikiki); cold-water summer swell, certified instructor + wetsuit.","bookable_category":"surf school / Viator (guided-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://pariwana-hostel.com/en/blog/2025/10/07/paragliding-in-lima-a-complete-guide-to-flying-over-the-costa-verde/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided surf school on the Miraflores/Barranco beach breaks (Makaha/Waikiki); cold-water summer swell, certified instructor + wetsuit.","commission":"affiliate 4-8%"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I actually get a table at Maido, Central or Kjolle?","a":"Book weeks ahead — the tables are the binding constraint, not the hotel. Central, Maido and Kjolle open reservations on a rolling monthly/multi-week basis and sell out, so the culinary itinerary must be built reservation-first; grey winter is fine because the dining is indoors.","source":"ohlalima.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What can I see in Lima in a day or two?","a":"More than you''d expect for a gateway city. Walk to Huaca Pucllana (a ~200–700 AD adobe pyramid in Miraflores), the Convento de San Francisco (founded 1540) catacombs in the UNESCO Centro Histórico, and the Larco Museum''s 5,000-year pre-Columbian collection in an 18th-century mansion.","source":"kaypiperutours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Lima good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — the base is bohemian Barranco, Lima''s most walkable, romantic district, home to the Puente de los Suspiros (\"Bridge of Sighs\") and to Hotel B, a restored 1914 Belle Époque arts-mansion that is the city''s only Relais & Châteaux.","source":"relaischateaux.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Lima?","a":"Urban street crime, not any activity. Stay in Miraflores, Barranco and San Isidro; use only registered radio-taxis, ride-hail apps or hotel transfers — never an unmarked street taxi, the classic express-kidnapping setup (forced ATM withdrawals over 1–3 hours). Use in-bank ATMs and keep valuables out of sight.","source":"bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lima Peru Travel Guide 2026 — World''s #1 Restaurant, Pre-Inca Ruins & Barranco | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Lima, Peru: the world''s #1 restaurant (Maido), Central, Kjolle and La Mar; pre-Inca Huaca Pucllana, Larco Museum and Pachacamac; bohemian Barranco; luxury Belmond & Relais & Chateaux stays; and clear L2 safety with zone/taxi coaching.","slug":"lima-peru","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":["en","es-PE"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Lima","mejores restaurantes Lima","Barranco Miraflores","Puente de los Suspiros","tour Huaca Pucllana","Museo Larco","Pachacámac desde Lima","parapente Costa Verde Lima","mejor época para viajar a Lima","cebicherías Lima","pisco sour Lima"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Miraflores Park, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"82-room clifftop Pacific-Riviera flagship in Miraflores; boutique service + full-luxury amenities; Lima''s iconic ultra address and a Belmond = Virtuoso-preferred flag (CLAUDE.md moat)","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Fora (Amex FHR-listed)","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso-preferred / consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hotel B","why_ultra":"Lima''s only Relais & Chateaux - restored 1914 Belle Epoque arts-mansion in Barranco, connected to the Lucia de la Puente gallery; the romance/honeymoon ultra pick","earning":"on application / Fora or Relais & Chateaux consortia where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Country Club Lima Hotel","why_ultra":"five-star 1927 San Isidro landmark (California-colonial, national heritage), Leading Hotels of the World; award-winning Perroquet + SUMMUM-winning English Bar Pisco Sour; living-history grandeur","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Fora / LHW Leaders Club where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"LHW/consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"JW Marriott Hotel Lima","why_ultra":"oceanfront Miraflores tower on the Costa Verde clifftop, steps from Larcomar/Malecon; best-located branded-luxury oceanfront with Bonvoy + STARS/Luminous eligibility","earning":"on application / Marriott STARS/Luminous or Fora where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS/Luminous amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Lima, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-12.0464,"lng":-77.0428}}'::jsonb, 58),
