airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"gray-whale HARD window ~mid-Jan-mid-Mar (calving lagoon)","second_peak":"sardine run / striped-marlin bait ball, mid-Oct-Dec","shoulder":"late Dec-early Jan (arrival), late Mar-Apr (tail-end)","green":"May-Sep (off-season, hot, hurricane-exposed)","booking_window_lead_time":"6-12 months (tiny whale-camp capacity, both windows sell out early)","out_of_season_fill":"minimal; sport fishing + birding fill edges","holiday_event_peaks":["US/Canada winter escape overlaps gray-whale peak"],"campaign_start_trigger":"gray-whale 9-12 months out; marlin/sardine-run by mid-summer for Oct-Dec"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Gray-whale calving-lagoon encounter","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator; net-rate red","name":"Barrier-island whale-camp overnight","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Mangrove / birding skiff","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Snorkel-with-striped-marlin bait ball (sardine run)","si":"ocean"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"luxury","commission":"operator/wholesale","name":"Striped-marlin liveaboard (Nautilus)","si":"ocean"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is gray-whale season in Magdalena Bay?","a":"The hard window is roughly mid-January to mid-March, when mothers and calves fill the calving lagoon; whales arrive late Dec–early Jan and linger to April. Mag Bay''s grays are famously \"friendly,\" often approaching the pangas — book the tiny whale-camp capacity 6–12 months ahead.","source":"seakayakadventures.com / randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I snorkel the striped-marlin bait balls?","a":"Yes, from about mid-October to December — but it''s an advanced open-water activity. You''re offshore in current among fast-moving marlin and sea lions driving sardines to the surface, so it''s for confident, fit snorkelers and freedivers with specialist operators only.","source":"magdalenabaywhales.com / divernet.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Where do I stay — are there resorts?","a":"No resorts — the accurate options are a barrier-island whale camp (glamping, 1–7 nights, ~$650+ for a 1-night all-in) or basic hotels in Puerto San Carlos and López Mateos. The camp is part of the experience: whales from shore, and nothing between you and the lagoon.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the bait-ball snorkel dangerous?","a":"It is not a beginner activity. The sardine run happens offshore in current among fast predators, so go only with specialist operators, follow the guide''s positioning rules and never touch the wildlife; if you dive elsewhere in Baja, the nearest chambers are La Paz and Cabo San Lucas with 18–24 h no-fly.","source":"divernet.com / sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Magdalena Bay — Gray-Whale Lagoon & Striped-Marlin Sardine Run | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Magdalena Bay, Baja California Sur: gray-whale calving lagoon (Jan-Mar) and the striped-marlin bait-ball sardine run (Oct-Dec). Whale-camp stays, seasons, safe-panga guidance.","primary_keywords":["Magdalena Bay whale watching","gray whale Magdalena Bay","striped marlin bait ball","Baja sardine run"],"long_tail":["gray whale season Magdalena Bay 2026","snorkel with striped marlin Baja","Magdalena Bay whale camp","Puerto San Carlos whale watching","how to get to Magdalena Bay from Los Cabos"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ballena gris Bahia Magdalena","avistamiento de ballenas Puerto San Carlos","marlin rayado Bahia Magdalena","corrida de la sardina Baja","campamento de ballenas Bahia Magdalena"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","ocean"],"ultra":[{"what":"National Geographic / Lindblad expedition cruise to Magdalena Bay (sea-based); or Los Cabos/East Cape ultra property as pre/post base","why_ultra":"small-ship expedition w/ naturalists is the only refined product on the bay; no land ultra exists here (nearest = Los Cabos/East Cape 3.5-6 h away)","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso; expedition-cruise lines carry advisor commission","virtuoso_value_add":"shipboard credit/expedition perks via preferred programs, or resort credit at Los Cabos base","mor":"resale via host-Virtuoso / cruise-wholesale only; Magdalena Bay lodging itself is NOT ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Magdalena Bay, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.6167,"lng":-112.1}}'::jsonb, 61),
  ('mahahual-mexico', '10S', 'Mahahual (Costa Maya & Banco Chinchorro)', 'Mexico', 'The largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"liveaboard","diveglobal"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Banco Chinchorro - largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere; biosphere 144,000 ha; ~25x10 mi","~80-90 min (some ops ~2.5h) boat from Mahahual; ~200 shipwrecks; permit-restricted (op handles permit)","Best viz May-Sep (~15-30m); crocodile-encounter season Jun 1-Sep 30 (XTC = sole federal permit)","Overnight = palafito stilt-hut on Cayo Centro (legalized 2010; no services) - the liveaboard-style product","Costa Maya cruise port (2nd-largest in Caribbean Mexico, up to ~20k cruisers) = OUT of TWW cruise scope"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","dan_emergency":"+1-919-684-9111","advisory_level":"L2","nearest_chamber":"Costamed, COZUMEL (DAN-certified) - Mahahual clinic has NO chamber; long medevac from Chinchorro","nearest_trauma":"Chetumal (Hospital General, south) or evac to Cancun","malaria":"NONE in tourist zone; dengue present","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"Jun-Nov, peak Aug-Oct","dive_no_fly":"18-24h (DAN)","special_rule":"REMOTE-MEDEVAC - dive conservative; permitted+certified op only; croc encounter handler-led, max 6/trip","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dive peak May-Sep (viz ~15-30m; croc encounter hard window Jun 1-Sep 30)","shoulder":"Apr and Oct edges","green":"Nov-Mar (wind/swell; Chinchorro often blown out - fall back to Costa Maya/Xcalak reef)","booking_lead":"4-6 months for permit-limited summer Chinchorro/croc product (permit scarcity = longer lead than a general reef trip)","off_season_specials":"winter Nov-Mar: Costa Maya/Xcalak mainland-reef dive days + no-fly beach fill-the-beds (lean Xcalak, south of the cruise port)","event_peaks":"croc window Jun 1-Sep 30; (Costa Maya cruise day-crowds peak Sep-Dec, busiest Nov, Wed/Thu - OUT of TWW scope, plan dive departures around it)","campaign_start":"live by Dec-Jan, ~4-6 months ahead of the May-Sep dive window; run a winter Xcalak-reef value campaign for Nov-Mar fill-the-beds"},"jewels":[{"name":"Chinchorro overnight palafito expedition (Cayo Centro)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"multi-day dive expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://pepedivemahahual.com/en/diving/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"on application (liveaboard-reseller/dive-op host)"},{"name":"~200-wreck atoll dives","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"wreck/wall diving","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20% / on application"},{"name":"Chinchorro day-boat 2-3 tank + Cayo Centro","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / affiliate"},{"name":"Costa Maya / Xcalak reef diving","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amigosdelmar.net/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20%"},{"name":"Wild American-crocodile in-water encounter (XTC)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","bookable_category":"expert-guided wildlife","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/crocs/croc-encounters/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","si":"expedition","blurb":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / on application; XTC sole permit"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for diving Mahahual?","a":"Remote medevac - the load-bearing risk. Mahahual has NO hyperbaric chamber; the nearest DAN-certified chamber is in Cozumel, a multi-hour transit from a Chinchorro site ~25 miles offshore. Dive conservatively, hold no-fly 18-24h, and treat DCS as a logistics problem.","source":"costamed.com.mx","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Mahahual and Chinchorro?","a":"May-September - the counterintuitive answer: calmest seas, best visibility (~15-30m) and the crocodile season (Jun 1-Sep 30), even though it overlaps the rainy/hurricane months. Winter (Nov-Mar) sees more wind and Chinchorro is often blown out.","source":"coralrealm.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I day-dive Banco Chinchorro, and how?","a":"Yes - most Mahahual/Xcalak operators run day-trips for certified divers: a 2-tank ($275) or 3-tank ($325) day with a Cayo Centro stop, an 80-90-minute crossing each way. The operator handles the limited federal permit when you book; May-September has the calmest seas.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can you really swim with wild crocodiles at Chinchorro?","a":"Yes - it''s the only legally permitted in-water wild-crocodile encounter on Earth, and only XTC Dive Center holds the federal permit. The season is a hard window of June 1 to September 30, capped at 6 people (2 in the water with the handler at a time), flotation device required. Book far ahead.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What is the Banco Chinchorro liveaboard experience actually like?","a":"It''s a stilt-hut expedition, not a cruise ship. Multi-day trips overnight in a palafito on Cayo Centro - a basic 2x2m stilt-deck fishing hut with hammocks and no services - legalized in 2010. It''s the closest access to the remote walls and ~200 wrecks; permit-scarce, so book the specialist operator well ahead.","source":"pepedivemahahual.com","si_tag":"liveaboard"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mahahual & Banco Chinchorro: Atoll Diving Guide","meta_description":"Mahahual is the gateway to Banco Chinchorro - the Northern Hemisphere''s largest coral atoll: ~200 wrecks, croc encounters, and the remote-chamber realities.","slug":"mahahual-mexico","primary_keyword":"Banco Chinchorro diving","long_tail":["Mahahual Banco Chinchorro dive","Chinchorro liveaboard palafito","Chinchorro crocodile snorkel XTC","Costa Maya diving","Xcalak scuba diving"],"search_language":"es","local_keywords":["buceo Banco Chinchorro","Mahahual buceo Costa Maya","encuentro con cocodrilos Xcalak","buceo Xcalak","atolon Chinchorro liveaboard palafito"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister - commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution, dated 2026-05-29) - freely bookable; the real planning is dive-medevac (nearest chamber Cozumel), not crime; MXN currency, dive prices often USD-quoted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-30","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; Banco Chinchorro moat = largest N-Hemisphere atoll (~200 wrecks) + sole permitted wild-crocodile encounter (XTC); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","name":"liveaboard","status":"live","note":"overnight-palafito multi-day on Cayo Centro (stilt-hut, not a cruise ship)"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private crewed Chinchorro dive charter / private palafito buy-out","why_ultra":"exclusive-use permitted multi-day atoll expedition - the rarest dive product in Mexican waters (permit-scarce, ~200 wrecks, sole-group access)","earning":"on application (dive-op/charter host / liveaboard-reseller)","virtuoso_value_add":"none formal (specialist dive charter, not a consortia hotel)","mor":"commission-on-net, agent-of-record; no net-rate resale"},{"name":"Nearest branded ultra = Riviera Maya (Mayakoba: Rosewood/Banyan Tree; Maroma A Belmond)","why_ultra":"n/a locally - branded-residence ultra sits far north; route ultra client Mahahual-for-dive + Riviera-Maya-for-stay","earning":"via host-Virtuoso (see Playa del Carmen / Puerto Morelos dossiers)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade / breakfast / resort credit (per those dossiers)","mor":"commission-on-net"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Mahahual (Costa Maya & Banco Chinchorro), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":18.7167,"lng":-87.7167}}'::jsonb, 62),
  ('manaus-amazon-brazil', '10S', 'Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon', 'Brazil', 'Where two great rivers meet', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"adventure","river","romance","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_medical":"192","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/brazil-travel-advisory.html","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":{"international":"MAO (Eduardo Gomes International, Manaus) — direct Miami + Panama City","domestic":"MAO — São Paulo / Brasília / Belém via LATAM, Gol, Azul"},"remote_flag":true,"malaria":"low in urban Manaus, real in deep-forest lodges — prophylaxis a lodge+season decision with a travel clinic","vaccinations":["yellow fever (required-in-practice, all Manaus travelers, ≥10 days pre-travel, single lifetime dose)","routine (DTP, MMR, polio, hep A/B) up to date"],"water":"bottled / lodge-treated only (no untreated river or tap water)","caveats":["High-vs-low water: the trip changes with the season — set expectations","Yellow fever vaccine required-in-practice ≥10 days pre-travel","Malaria prophylaxis for deep-forest lodges; dengue/Zika/chikungunya year-round, active 2026","Jungle-lodge remoteness — hours by river from Manaus hospitals; confirm evac insurance","Manaus urban crime — vetted transport, discreet valuables, night-area discipline","River safety — lifejackets on all transfers/excursions"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_high_water":"March–August, peaking Jun–Jul — flooded-forest / canoe-the-canopy Amazon","peak_low_water":"September–February — river beaches, hiking, peacock-bass fishing","inflection":"mid–late April (high-water established; Jun–Jul lodge/riverboat inventory locks)","fire_date":"late March (high-water curve-start − 1–2 wks); mirror fire date late August for the low-water product","off_season_fill":"none true — opposite peaks mean year-round sell; pivot copy to whichever product the calendar delivers","note":"the product itself changes with water level — high-water = flooded-forest canoeing; low-water = beaches/hiking/fishing; itineraries must state which"},"jewels":[{"name":"Meeting of the Waters (Encontro das Águas)","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Manaus-attractions/Meeting-of-Waters/d4441-a6911","hook":"the 6-km line where the warm dark Rio Negro and the pale cooler Solimões run side by side without mixing, the signature Amazon spectacle","si":"adventure","blurb":"the 6-km line where the warm dark Rio Negro and the pale cooler Solimões run side by side without mixing, the signature Amazon spectacle","commission":"DMC / tour affiliate half-day; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Jungle-lodge canopy + night walk","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.rainforestcruises.com/lodges/mirante-do-gaviao","hook":"the core lodge product: elevated canopy walkways by day, spotlight forest walk by night, naturalist naming birds, insects, tree frogs","si":"adventure","blurb":"the core lodge product: elevated canopy walkways by day, spotlight forest walk by night, naturalist naming birds, insects, tree frogs","commission":"DMC lodge package (AOR)"},{"name":"Presidente Figueiredo waterfalls + river-caves","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Manaus/Presidente-Figueiredo-Waterfalls-Day-Trip-from-Manaus/d4441-2484MAOFALLS","hook":"the \"Land of Waterfalls\" 107 km / ~1.5 h north of Manaus: Iracema and Araras falls, Lagoa Cristalina, and river-caves home to bats, turtles","si":"adventure","blurb":"the \"Land of Waterfalls\" 107 km / ~1.5 h north of Manaus: Iracema and Araras falls, Lagoa Cristalina, and river-caves home to bats, turtles","commission":"DMC / tour affiliate full-day; municipal fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Night caiman-spotting + piranha fishing","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"comfort","source":"https://offroadstravel.com/home/amazon-brazil-tour/","hook":"the two classic after-dark / on-water lodge excursions; spotlight the shallows for orange caiman eyeshine, drop a hand-line for piranha","si":"adventure","blurb":"the two classic after-dark / on-water lodge excursions; spotlight the shallows for orange caiman eyeshine, drop a hand-line for piranha","commission":"DMC lodge package (AOR)"},{"name":"Amazon riverboat expedition (Iberostar Grand Amazon)","si_tag":"river","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.rainforestcruises.com/cruises/iberostar-grand-amazon","hook":"72-cabin 5★ all-inclusive expedition boat, 4/5/8-day Solimões + Negro itineraries from Manaus, English-guided excursions, ending at the Meeting of the Waters","si":"river","blurb":"72-cabin 5★ all-inclusive expedition boat, 4/5/8-day Solimões + Negro itineraries from Manaus, English-guided excursions, ending at the Meeting of the Waters","commission":"DMC / consortia / cruise affiliate; all-inclusive package"},{"name":"Small-group expedition riverboat (Katerre / Jacaré-Açu)","si_tag":"river","tier":"premier","source":"https://amazonastravel.com.br/expedicao-katerre-i.html","hook":"low-impact small-group boats, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas / Jaú, full board with drinks, bilingual guide, park entries, Novo Airão embarkation","si":"river","blurb":"low-impact small-group boats, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas / Jaú, full board with drinks, bilingual guide, park entries, Novo Airão embarkation","commission":"DMC / operator (Amazonas by Viverde) net/commission package"},{"name":"Anavilhanas archipelago","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://national-parks.org/brazil/anavilhanas-national-park/","hook":"the second-largest river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the second-largest river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","commission":"DMC / lodge / riverboat; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Pink river dolphins (boto), Novo Airão","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/swimming-with-pink-dolphins-in-brazil/","hook":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","commission":"DMC day-trip / lodge excursion; platform-regulated"},{"name":"Indigenous / ribeirinho community visit","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amazontourmanaus.com/manaus-amazon/the-amazon-rainforest/anavilhanas-national-park/item162","hook":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","si":"wildlife","blurb":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","commission":"vetted DMC / operator AOR only (ethical, community-consenting)"},{"name":"Teatro Amazonas opera house","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Theatre","hook":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","si":"Romance & Honeymoons / Culture","blurb":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","commission":"DMC / city-tour affiliate; performance/visit ticket non-commissionable"},{"name":"Design jungle-lodge honeymoon (Mirante do Gavião / Anavilhanas)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.here-away.com/mirantedogaviaoamazonlodge","hook":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","commission":"DMC lodge package / consortia (AOR)"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"meta_title":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon Travel Guide 2026 — Meeting of the Waters, Jungle Lodges & Amazon Cruises | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Manaus Amazônia o que fazer","Encontro das Águas passeio","cruzeiro Rio Negro Amazonas","melhores lodges de selva na Amazônia","botos cor-de-rosa Novo Airão","cachoeiras Presidente Figueiredo","Teatro Amazonas visita","vacina febre amarela Manaus","Manaus é seguro para turistas","lua de mel na Amazônia","arquipélago de Anavilhanas","Amazônia cheia e vazante melhor época"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Mirante do Gavião Amazon Lodge","lane":"Fora/consortia","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra","note":"12-suite design lodge, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas edge"},{"name":"Anavilhanas Jungle Lodge","lane":"consortia/Fora","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier","note":"glass-wall bungalows, floating bar, pool, spa"},{"name":"Juma Amazon Lodge","lane":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"comfort","note":"stilted treetop bungalows ~15m, solar-powered"},{"name":"Iberostar Grand Amazon (riverboat)","lane":"consortia/cruise affiliate","mor":"consortia/operator","tier":"premier","note":"72-cabin all-inclusive expedition; verify consortia lane"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.119,"lng":-60.0217}}'::jsonb, 63),
  ('manuel-antonio-costa-rica', '10S', 'Manuel Antonio', 'Costa Rica', 'Sloths, monkeys and Pacific cliffs', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Costa Rica', '{"tropical","expedition","wildlife"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Manuel Antonio NP is open Wed–Mon 07:00–16:00, CLOSED every Tuesday; adult entry US$18, child (2–12) US$5, under-2 free; advance online ticket + passport number required.","One of few places to see all of Costa Rica''s iconic wildlife at a beach: 2- & 3-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (90%+ of visits), endangered Central American squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans.","Two park beaches: crescent Playa Manuel Antonio (calm, turquoise — best/safest swim) and longer, choppier Playa Espadilla Sur.","Access: ~2.5–3 hr / ~168 km drive from San José (SJO), OR ~25-min domestic flight to Quepos–Manuel Antonio (XQP) on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways + 15 km / 25-min transfer.","Cliffside-resort belt (Arenas del Mar, Makanda, Gaia, Tulemar) makes it a top romance/honeymoon hub; hillside villas make it a strong family/multi-gen hub."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital Metropolitano Quepos (private, 24-hr, marina) + public Max Terán Valls Hospital; serious cases to San José major hospitals (~2.5–3 hr) with air evac available","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"l2_disclosure":true,"advisory_note":"US Level 2 Exercise Increased Caution (reissued 2026-04-02); clean L2, no L4 zone near Manuel Antonio/Quepos; standard caution — petty crime, don''t display wealth, avoid poorly lit beaches at night, enroll in STEP","air_access_verified":"SJO gateway; XQP (Quepos–Manuel Antonio) ~25-min domestic flight on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways, or ~2.5–3 hr drive from SJO","riptide":"HARD FLAG — rip currents are the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (>80% of drownings); most beaches unguarded. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches (park cove safest), heed red flags, never swim alone; if caught, swim parallel to shore.","wildlife":"Bold habituated monkeys/raccoons/coatis raid food — no feeding, seal food, don''t leave bags unattended","dengue":"Year-round mosquito-borne risk (higher green season May–Nov); no widely available traveler vaccine — DEET/picaridin, cover at dawn/dusk, screened/AC rooms","water":"Tap water in San José & major tourist areas (incl. Manuel Antonio/Quepos) treated and generally safe; sensitive stomachs / remote lodges use bottled/filtered","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late October–early November","peak":"mid-December–April (Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa ~1 yr lead)","fire_date":"2026-10-17","shoulder":"May–November (green-season value)","green":"May–November (afternoon rain; lush, lower rates)","booking_lead":"3–8 weeks normal peak; ~1 year for Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa (lead pressure on cliffside-resort + villa beds)","off_season_specials":"green-season resort/villa discounts + whale-watching backfill (Jul–Oct/Nov Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks)","event_peaks":["Whale season Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep)","Whale season Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb)","Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa (Easter)"],"operational_note":"Manuel Antonio NP closed every Tuesday — route park visit Wed–Mon; slot waterfalls/catamaran/mangrove on Tuesday"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Manuel Antonio (in-park)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s best and safest swim/snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","bookable_category":"guided park tour / DIY ticket","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mustseespots.com/costa-rica/articles/manuel-antonio-national-park-beaches-wildlife-trails-explained/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s best and safest swim/snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Playa Biesanz","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Small jungle-backed calm cove on Quepos Point — the local''s-choice calm-swim/kayak/snorkel beach away from crowds.","bookable_category":"DIY + gear / guided kayak-snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Small jungle-backed calm cove on Quepos Point — the local''s-choice calm-swim/kayak/snorkel beach away from crowds.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"thin/DIY concierge add-on; small guided kayak-snorkel via affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Catamaran sunset + snorkel","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~4-hr coastal catamaran with snorkeling, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","bookable_category":"catamaran tour / private charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/Snorkeling_Tours.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~4-hr coastal catamaran with snorkeling, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; DMC/host-IATA for private charter","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","bookable_category":"guided day tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Damas Island mangrove kayak","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","bookable_category":"half-day kayak tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/tours/Half-Day-Kayak-Damas-Mangroves.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + local operator; host-IATA private","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Rainmaker canopy + hanging bridges","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","bookable_category":"guided canopy/bridges tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","when":"year-round","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Quepos marina sportfishing","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","bookable_category":"charter","tier":"premier","source":"https://costaricaexperts.com/destinations/manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"host-IATA / private-charter agent-of-record; premium day rates","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Marino Ballena / Uvita)","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","bookable_category":"guided whale-watching boat tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://puravidamoms.com/whale-watching-uvita-tour-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + host-IATA; Marino Ballena entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"National Park wildlife walk (sloths + 4 monkey species)","si_tag":"Wildlife","status":"future","hook":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","bookable_category":"guided park wildlife tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventuretourscostarica.com/blog/spotting-sloths-monkeys-your-manuel-antonio-wildlife-guide + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio National Park open on Tuesday?","a":"No — the park is closed every Tuesday, year-round including holidays. It is open Wednesday–Monday 07:00–16:00; adult entry is $18, children 2–12 $5, under-2 free, and advance online ticket purchase with your passport number is required — route the park visit Wed–Mon.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you see whales near Manuel Antonio?","a":"Yes — nearby Marino Ballena / Uvita has two humpback seasons. Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks run Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep) and Northern-Hemisphere humpbacks Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb), a rare draw spanning both the green and dry seasons, ~45–60 min south by guided boat tour.","source":"puravidamoms.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — it''s one of Costa Rica''s premier romance hubs. The cliffside-resort belt above the beach, led by adults-only Makanda by the Sea ~100 m above the ocean, defines the honeymoon identity, while Arenas del Mar is the only true beachfront luxury resort with two private beaches.","source":"oyster.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you really see sloths and monkeys at the beach?","a":"Yes — it''s one of very few places anywhere you reliably can. Two- and three-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (on 90%+ of visits), the endangered Central American squirrel monkey, howlers, coatis and toucans all live inside a compact, walkable national park where the rainforest meets the sand.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife-—-future"},{"q":"What''s the biggest safety risk in Manuel Antonio?","a":"Pacific rip currents — the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (over 80% of drownings), on mostly unguarded beaches. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches (the calm park cove of Playa Manuel Antonio is safest), heed red flags, never swim alone, and if caught, swim parallel to shore.","source":"crie.cr, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the monkeys a problem in the park?","a":"They can be — capuchins, raccoons and coatis are bold and habituated and will raid open bags and grab food. Don''t feed wildlife, keep food sealed and bags zipped, and don''t leave belongings unattended on the beach.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica Travel Guide — Sloths, Rainforest Beaches, Cliffside Resorts & Quepos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"See sloths and monkeys at a Pacific beach, base on the Quepos cliffs for romance or in a villa for family, and do Manuel Antonio well, safely, and at the right time — park hours, riptide safety, whales, catamarans and waterfalls.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","long_tail_en":["Manuel Antonio National Park hours 2026","is Manuel Antonio open on Tuesday","best time to visit Manuel Antonio Costa Rica","Manuel Antonio sloths and monkeys guide","Manuel Antonio riptide beach safety","SJO to Quepos flight Manuel Antonio","Manuel Antonio cliffside honeymoon resorts","Manuel Antonio villas with pool family","Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip from Manuel Antonio","Uvita whale watching season from Manuel Antonio"],"local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio","playas Manuel Antonio","qué hacer en Quepos","avistamiento de ballenas Uvita Marino Ballena","cataratas Nauyaca desde Manuel Antonio","kayak manglares isla Damas","perezosos y monos Manuel Antonio","hoteles de lujo Manuel Antonio","vuelo San José a Quepos","horario Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio precio entrada"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Arenas del Mar (Böÿ Collection / Cayuga)","why_ultra":"The only true beachfront luxury resort in Manuel Antonio — private ridge, two secluded beaches (golf-cart access), rainforest all around, strong sustainability, ocean-view suites with plunge pools. The apex property.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity block; agent-of-record commission","consortia_value_add":"upgrade, breakfast/resort credit, early/late, VIP welcome (confirm current program)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record","tier":"luxury / ultra"},{"name":"Makanda by the Sea","why_ultra":"Adults-only (16+), ~100 m above the ocean on 12 acres of rainforest gardens — the definitive Manuel Antonio honeymoon/romance property; small, private, view-forward.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit where program allows (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Gaia Hotel & Reserve","why_ultra":"Eco-chic adults-oriented 22-room private-reserve hillside hotel; 500-thread-count linens, wellness + service focus.","earning":"consortia/agent rate","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"premier / luxury"},{"name":"Tulemar Resort (+ private villas)","why_ultra":"Gated hillside estate with its own private sandy beach, 4 pools, concierge, spa, and a portfolio of private villas — the best resort-serviced villa play for families/multi-gen.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + villa MoR","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit + villa perks (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record + villa direct-contract","tier":"premier / luxury (villas: luxury/ultra)"},{"name":"Preferred / luxury hillside villas","why_ultra":"Private ocean-view villas (chef/staff, pools, 2–8 br) — the whole-property-buyout ultra lane for honeymooners + multi-gen groups.","earning":"villa MoR + agent-of-record","consortia_value_add":"n/a (villa direct-contract perks vary)","mor":"direct-contract / villa specialist (host-IATA)","tier":"luxury / ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.392,"lng":-84.137}}'::jsonb, 64),
  ('mazamitla-mexico', '10S', 'Mazamitla', 'Mexico', 'Chalet cabañas in a pine-oak Sierra', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"expedition","family","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Pueblo Mágico (2005) at ~2,200 m in southern Jalisco, ~124–135 km / ~2 hr from Guadalajara; ''Switzerland of Mexico'' (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Cool year-round (~15°C avg; ~7–26°C) — a magnet for Guadalajara residents, esp. summer (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazamitla, Accessed 2026-07-04)","El Salto waterfall ~35 m in Los Cazos (private, ~US$1, ~45-min forest hike or horse ~M$250) (Source: zonaturistica.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Signature chalet cabañas (e.g., Cabañas Monteverde: kitchens, fireplaces, daily firewood) (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Canopy/zipline + six-hanging-bridge tours (Green Forest Tours); La Zanja 1977 town forest (Source: theguadalajarapost.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"No major trauma hospital in town; nearest full ER/trauma is Guadalajara ~2 hr / ~124–135 km back down mountain road; local clinic for minor cases; air-evac to US for critical cases","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":false,"tourist_zone_carveout":"none","air_access_verified":"via GDL ~2 hr ground (not into a carve-out); approach via Hwy 405 (advisory-designated route)","advisory_note":"Advisory names Mazamitla as a specific EXCEPTION to the Hwy-110 restriction and directs ''travel via Highway 405 only'' — stronger than a blanket exclusion, but still NOT a named safe-zone carve-out; ruling holds at no-Book","malaria":"none","dengue":"very low at ~2,200 m (above Aedes aegypti elevation ceiling)","yellow_fever":"not required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Domestic-holiday & weekend peaks — summer (GDL heat escape) + Semana Santa + Christmas/New-Year + long weekends; cool ~15°C year-round draw","waterfall_flow_peak":"October–December (fullest El Salto flow, post-rains)","shoulder":"Non-holiday weekdays / shoulder months","green":"Deep off-holiday midweeks (softest domestic demand)","booking_lead":"Weeks–months for Semana Santa/summer/Christmas/long-weekend cabañas; midweek walk-up-easy; largely direct/domestic","event_peaks":"Semana Santa, summer school holidays, Christmas–New-Year, Mexican puentes","campaign_start":"''Cool-mountain weekend from Guadalajara'' ahead of summer + Semana Santa; waterfall-flow (Oct–Dec) into fall"},"jewels":[{"name":"El Salto waterfall (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","bookable_category":"site entry (~US$1) + guide/horse","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zonaturistica.com/en/things-to-do/jalisco/mazamitla/the-salto-waterfall (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","commission":"day-tour or curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"La Zanja town forest","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","bookable_category":"free/low-cost","tier":"essential","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","commission":"curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Canopy + six hanging bridges (Green Forest Tours)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","bookable_category":"operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","when":"year-round","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Chalet cabañas (Cabañas Monteverde)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","bookable_category":"direct (domestic)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","commission":"curated-recommend (direct-only)","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Enchanted Garden (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","bookable_category":"site entry + rentals","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","commission":"day-tour / curated","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Los Cazos ATV + horseback","si_tag":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future","hook":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","bookable_category":"licensed operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"Adventure / Ecotourism","blurb":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book a stay in Mazamitla through TravelWell?","a":"No — it is content-only, recommended only as a licensed day/weekend trip from the Guadalajara carve-out. Jalisco is US State Dept Level 3 (May 29, 2026) and Mazamitla is not one of the four named carve-outs; notably, though, the advisory names Mazamitla as an exception to the Highway 110 restriction and permits access \"via Highway 405 only.\" book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The ~2-hour mountain road transfer, not the town''s street crime (which is low — a domestic family town). The drive from Guadalajara leaves the GDL safe zone, even on the advisory-approved Highway 405, which is the hold reason; use licensed daytime transport only, and note the nearest full trauma hospital is ~2 hr back in Guadalajara.","source":"travel.state.gov / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is there to do at El Salto waterfall?","a":"Hike to it. The ~35 m El Salto falls in Los Cazos are reached by a ~45-minute forest trail (or a horse, ~M$250) to a wooden overlook, entry ~US$1, with the fullest flow October–December after the rains. Sturdy footwear, and turn back in weather.","source":"zonaturistica.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Mazamitla good for a family weekend?","a":"Yes — it is the classic Guadalajara family escape. The product is a wooden chalet cabaña with a full kitchen and fireplace (Cabañas Monteverde delivers firewood daily) in a cool ~15°C pine-oak Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m; cabañas sell out for Semana Santa, summer and Christmas, so book weeks to months ahead.","source":"travelagewest.com / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"What adventure activities are on offer?","a":"Zip, ride and cross bridges. Green Forest Tours runs a 3-hour zipline and a 2-hour six-hanging-bridge walk, plus ATV, horseback and mountain-biking through the forest and Los Cazos. Use licensed operators with helmet/harness checks — evac to Guadalajara is ~2 hr, so injuries carry a distance penalty.","source":"theguadalajarapost.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"adventure"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mazamitla Travel Guide — Jalisco''s ''Mexican Switzerland'' Cabaña Mountain Pueblo Mágico | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Jalisco''s cool pine-forest Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m — chalet cabañas, the El Salto waterfall, canopy tours, and straight guidance: a Level-3-interior day/weekend trip from Guadalajara (Hwy 405), not a bookable base.","slug":"mazamitla-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mazamitla Mexico travel guide","long_tail":["Mazamitla from Guadalajara day trip","El Salto waterfall Mazamitla","Mazamitla cabañas Monteverde","is Mazamitla safe","Mazamitla Suiza Mexicana things to do"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Mazamitla Pueblo Mágico","Mazamitla desde Guadalajara","cascada El Salto Mazamitla","cabañas en Mazamitla","Mazamitla la Suiza Mexicana","tirolesa puentes colgantes Mazamitla"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"future"},{"si":"family","status":"future"},{"si":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Mazamitla, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.9153,"lng":-103.0208}}'::jsonb, 65)
