ne into the flower festival; December holidays/Alumbrados compress again","off_season_fill":["April–May","September–November"],"fire_date":"Feria de las Flores: fire by ~2026-07-15 (curve-start − 1–2 wks); December Alumbrados: fire late November"},"jewels":[{"name":"Comuna 13 graffiti + escalators (guided transformation tour)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Medellin/Guided-Tour-of-Comuna-13-Medellin-with-Snacks-Included/d4563-473336P1 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The city''s most-visited site; murals, escalators that cut a 35-min climb to 6, community art, street food","si":"culture","blurb":"The city''s most-visited site; murals, escalators that cut a 35-min climb to 6, community art, street food","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"non-commissionable / activity affiliate (vetted community operator)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Metrocable to Parque Arví","si_tag":"CHER/GEA","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.medellin.travel/what-to-do-in-medellin-neighborhoods-culture-and-creative-tourism/?lang=en (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Public gondola over the barrios up to a high cloud-forest ecological park — social urbanism and a jaw-dropping ride","si":"CHER/GEA","blurb":"Public gondola over the barrios up to a high cloud-forest ecological park — social urbanism and a jaw-dropping ride","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"non-commissionable transit anchoring paid Arví add-ons","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Botero Plaza + Museo de Antioquia","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/comuna-13-medellin-2026-street-art-transformation-tour.htm (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","si":"culture","blurb":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC-guided downtown add-on / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Guatapé + El Peñol rock (740 steps) + zócalos","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Medellin/Guatape-and-Penol-Rock-Full-Day-Tour/d4563-6033P27 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","si":"expedition","blurb":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"day-trip operator affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Jardín & Jericó coffee pueblos + working-finca coffee tour","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","si":"expedition","blurb":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC / coffee-hacienda MoR stay","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Paragliding the Aburrá Valley (San Félix)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","si":"expedition","blurb":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC (operator-vetted only)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"El Poblado / Provenza & Manila dining","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","si":"culinary","blurb":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC dining add-ons / hotel F&B / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Feria de las Flores — silleteros (Jul 31–Aug 9, 2026)","si_tag":"RHN/CHER","tier":"comfort","source":"https://medellingroup.com/blog/feria-de-las-flores-2026-complete-guide-to-medellins-flower-festival (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","si":"RHN/CHER","blurb":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC festival packages + hotel/villa MoR","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Medellín a good place for a couples trip or honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for couples arriving together. El Poblado luxury apartments, rooftop-pool hotels and coffee-finca escapes are genuinely romantic. The plain caveat: the US Embassy links 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths in Medellín (Nov–Dec 2023) to dating-app-lured druggings, so the safe lane is partners who arrive together, not app meet-ups.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is Comuna 13 and is it worth visiting?","a":"Yes — Comuna 13 is Medellín''s most-visited site and the emblem of its turnaround. Outdoor public escalators installed in 2011 cut a 35-minute climb to 6 minutes; today the hillside barrio is a canvas of community murals, told on a guided walking tour (~$20–30). Go guided, daytime, as a group.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do you visit Guatapé and El Peñol rock from Medellín?","a":"Guatapé sits about 2 hours east, usually as a full-day trip. The headline is climbing El Peñol (Piedra del Peñol) via 740 steps — most reach the top in 15–25 minutes — over a reservoir dotted with islands, then wandering the brightly painted zócalo streets. Book a day-trip operator or DMC.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Medellín?","a":"The signature Medellín danger is dating-app drugging-and-robbery, not the headlines. The US Embassy is aware of 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths (Nov 1–Dec 31, 2023) involving scopolamine (\"burundanga\") — odorless, memory-erasing and lethal in large doses. Don''t meet app strangers alone, never leave a drink unattended, and meet only in public.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is climbing El Peñol''s 740 steps dangerous?","a":"It''s a steep but manageable self-guided climb — 740 steps, 15–25 minutes for most — though not for those with cardiac or mobility limits. Pace it, hydrate, and mind your footing on the descent. Paragliding over the Aburrá Valley, by contrast, should be flown only with certified, insured, safety-vetted operators.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Medellín & Antioquia Travel Guide 2026 — Comuna 13, Guatapé, Coffee Country | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-CO","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Medellín","Comuna 13 tour","Guatapé Peñol","Feria de las Flores","dónde hospedarse en Medellín","seguridad Medellín aplicaciones de citas"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"],"author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Medellín & Antioquia"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"The Charlee","location":"El Poblado","note":"Envy rooftop pool/bar, 360° valley views; most-photographed hotel in Colombia","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Diez Hotel Categoría Colombia","location":"El Poblado","note":"Colombian-art boutique, full-service spa","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Click Clack Hotel Medellín","location":"El Poblado","note":"Design-forward, artisan interiors, rooftop; Mr & Mrs Smith listed","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Luxury coffee-country haciendas (Hacienda Bambusa / Sazagua-tier)","location":"Antioquia / Coffee-Triangle-adjacent","note":"Rural ultra pairing","program":"MoR","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"NOTE — Four Seasons Casa Medina","location":"Bogotá (NOT Medellín)","note":"Do not misassign to Medellín","program":"n/a","price_tier":"$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Medellín & Antioquia, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":6.2442,"lng":-75.5812}}'::jsonb, 66),
  ('mendoza-argentina', '10S', 'Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina', 'Argentina', 'Malbec born a thousand metres up, poured under the', 'live', 'verified', 'restaurant', 'Northwest, Mendoza Wine & Iguazú', '{"culinary","romance","expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L1","advisory_updated":"2026-05-20","regional_exception":"Level 2 — city of Rosario only (~1,000 km from Mendoza)","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":false,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Mendoza El Plumerillo (MDZ) via Buenos Aires (AEP/EZE)","trauma":"excellent Mendoza private clinics (English-speaking); severe trauma escalates to Buenos Aires + international evac; carry medical/evac insurance","drink_drive":"always a designated driver or guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings","altitude":"Alta Montaña day trip ~2,700 m (mild); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is expedition-grade, guided + permitted","rafting":"Mendoza River (Potrerillos) Class II–IV; certified guides mandatory","water":"potable in Mendoza city/major towns; bottled/treated in remote areas","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"late Feb–April (harvest / Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia; 2026 central acts Mar 6–10) + autumn Mar–Apr","secondary_peak":"Oct–Nov (spring; ~15–25% below harvest rates)","inflection":"book icon wineries/lodges 3–4 months ahead of Feb–April peak; demand inflects at Vendimia-calendar release (Jan) and ~90 days out","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1–2 weeks — late Jan → mid-Feb for March/Vendimia trips; late Sept for Oct–Nov spring window","off_season_fill":"winter Jun–Aug — Andes ski (Los Penitentes/Penitentes, Jun–Sep) + Cacheuta thermal wellness + indoor-cellar tastings"},"jewels":[{"name":"Valle de Uco icon estates + long lunch (Zuccardi Piedra Infinita, Salentein + Kilka)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.mrwinery.com/tour/visit-zuccardi-piedra-infinita-and-have-lunch-at-bodega","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%"},{"name":"The Vines estate tasting + vine-side table","si_tag":"culinary+romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.scottdunn.com/us/argentina/hotels/the-vines-resort-spa","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","si":"culinary+romance","blurb":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC / lodge package 10–20%"},{"name":"Luján de Cuyo classic Malbec cellars","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/lujan-de-cuyo-from-mendoza-wine-route-2026-malbec-guide.htm","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","si":"culinary","blurb":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Catena Zapata pyramid + Blending Games","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mendoza/Catena-Zapata-Wine-Tour-from-Mendoza/d931-5693P18","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","si":"culinary","blurb":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"private-transport DMC/affiliate 4–20%"},{"name":"Maipú bike-and-wine + olive-oil & asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-travel-guide-2026-argentinas-wine-capital.htm","hook":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","si":"culinary","blurb":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Achaval-Ferrer single-vineyard Malbec","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-wine-tours-2026-best-wineries-tastings.htm","si":"culinary","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Sunrise hot-air balloon over the vineyards","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/argentina-l168992/hot-air-balloon-ride-over-mendoza-s-vineyards-wine-toast-t876044/","hook":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","si":"romance","blurb":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","commission":"affiliate 4–8% / DMC bundle"},{"name":"Cacheuta thermal springs","si_tag":"romance+wellness","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thewholeworldornothing.com/hot-springs-mendoza-cacheuta-thermal-baths/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","si":"romance+wellness","blurb":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC"},{"name":"Alta Montaña + Aconcagua viewpoint + Puente del Inca","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/mendoza-l673/andes-day-trip-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-t55889/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","si":"expedition","blurb":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%"},{"name":"Mendoza River rafting (Potrerillos)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/adventure-tourism-in-potrerillos-mendoza/","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 private vineyard villas on 1,500 acres + spa + vine-side dining","earning":"consortia commission + villa MoR","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Uco","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"modern estate rooms, pool + spa, working-vineyard finca","earning":"consortia / DMC commission","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Entre Cielos","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"design hotel in 3.2 ha Malbec vines + Hammam spa circuit","earning":"consortia / bedbank premium","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-32.8895,"lng":-68.8458}}'::jsonb, 67),
  ('merida-mexico', '10S', 'Mérida, Yucatán', 'Mexico', 'Mérida Yucatán travel guide', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"romance","expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Capital of Yucatán state and the peninsula''s cultural + medical hub; nicknamed ''La Ciudad Blanca'' (the White City).","Yucatán is US State Department Level 1 (Exercise Normal Precautions) — one of only two Level-1 Mexican states; the safest tier.","Heart of the restored-hacienda hotel circuit — Chablé, four Luxury Collection haciendas, Angsana Xcanatún — the region''s signature luxury supply.","Distinct Yucatecan cuisine (cochinita pibil, sopa de lima, mucbipollo) centered on the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls).","Gateway to cenote country, Celestún/Río Lagartos flamingos, Uxmal + Ruta Puuc, and Chichén Itzá; Gulf beach at Progreso ~35 min north."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Star Médica Mérida; Christus Muguerza Faro del Mayab; Centro Médico de las Américas (CMA); Clínica de Mérida — regional trauma/medical hub","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"MID — Mérida Manuel Crescencio Rejón International (direct US: DFW, IAH, MIA)","heat":"Hot-humid May–Sep; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F (38°C) — extreme-heat protocol on daytime ruin/cenote outings","water":"Bottled only (do not drink tap; use bottled for tooth-brushing)","malaria":"No malaria risk in Mérida / Yucatán tourist corridor; dengue present, chikungunya rising (2025–26) — mosquito precautions","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll 