al Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"~2026-10-25 (Hanal Pixán opening; late-Oct heat break + end of hurricane season lifts demand off baseline)","peak":"December–April (tightest Dec–March; dry-cool, low humidity)","fire_date":"2026-10-10","shoulder":"November; late April–early May","green":"May–September (hot-humid; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F/38°C; rains peak Jun–Sep)","booking_lead":"Hacienda weddings 6–12 months (advised 10–12); leisure 1–3 months, longer for Hanal Pixán week","off_season_specials":"Summer hacienda + mansion-boutique rate softening; cenote-and-spa ''White City in the Green Season'' packaging; indoor culture year-round","event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Festival de las Ánimas (Oct 25–Nov 2)","Mérida Fest (early-mid January; 2026 ran Jan 5–18)","Flamingo season Nov–Feb (Celestún / Río Lagartos)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Paseo de Montejo mansions (Casa Museo Montes Molina)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","bookable_category":"guided walking tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.kupi.com/en-ae/explore/mexico/merida/paseo-de-montejo","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local guide affiliate"},{"name":"Gran Museo del Mundo Maya","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","bookable_category":"entry + guided combo","tier":"essential","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/Merida_Mexico/Things_To_Do/El_Gran_Museo_del_Mundo_Maya_de_Mrida_65503/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","when":"December–April","commission":"affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Izamal — The Yellow Town + Convento de San Antonio","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","bookable_category":"private day-trip + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator commissionable"},{"name":"Uxmal + Ruta Puuc","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The connoisseur''s Chichén — grander, emptier","bookable_category":"guided ruin circuit","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Merida/UXMAL-ROUTE-HACIENDAS-AND-CENOTES/d5195-148085P1","si":"culture","blurb":"The connoisseur''s Chichén — grander, emptier","commission":"DMC/Viator commissionable"},{"name":"Chichén Itzá day-trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The bucket-list ruin, done heat-smart at dawn","bookable_category":"guided day-tour + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The bucket-list ruin, done heat-smart at dawn","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Mercado Lucas de Gálvez + cochinita pibil","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"All of Yucatán in one riot of color and smell","bookable_category":"food walking tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelyucatan.com/merida-itinerary/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"All of Yucatán in one riot of color and smell","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local affiliate + guide"},{"name":"Ixi''im at Chablé Yucatán (1,000-bottle tequila cellar)","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Dinner as a cellar tour","bookable_category":"dining within a stay","tier":"ultra","source":"https://yucatan.chablehotels.com/cuisine/ixiim/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culinary","blurb":"Dinner as a cellar tour","when":"year-round","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso (stay)"},{"name":"Hacienda-wedding circuit (Temozón/Santa Rosa/San José/Xcanatún/Sac Chich)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Married inside living history — chapel ruins + cenote gardens","bookable_category":"venue buyout + room block + planner","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.destinationweddings.com/hacienda-san-jose-a-luxury-collection-hotel-san-jose","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Married inside living history — chapel ruins + cenote gardens","when":"December–April","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso room block + wedding DMC"},{"name":"Rosas & Xocolate honeymoon suite","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"City-romance base with a rooftop and a story","bookable_category":"boutique hotel stay","tier":"premier","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/rosas-y-xocolate-a-luxury-food-and-lodging-icon-in-merida","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"City-romance base with a rooftop and a story","when":"December–April","commission":"Marriott Bonvoy/STARS — Fora/Virtuoso"},{"name":"Celestún flamingo biosphere boat safari","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Pink clouds at the edge of the Gulf","bookable_category":"guided day-trip + boat","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.girlwiththepassport.com/best-day-trips-from-merida-mexico/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Pink clouds at the edge of the Gulf","commission":"DMC/Viator (boat fee pass-through)"},{"name":"Río Lagartos + Las Coloradas","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Flamingos and rose-pink water in one frame","bookable_category":"long day-trip / overnight","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.girlwiththepassport.com/best-day-trips-from-merida-mexico/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Flamingos and rose-pink water in one frame","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC commissionable"},{"name":"Cuzamá / Homún cenote country (rail-cart)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"The most Indiana-Jones way to reach turquoise water","bookable_category":"guided cenote-country day-trip","tier":"comfort","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"The most Indiana-Jones way to reach turquoise water","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator (cenote entry pass-through)"},{"name":"Cenotes de Mucuyché / Santa Bárbara","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Both cenote personalities in one day — open + cavern","bookable_category":"private cenote tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/AttractionProductReview-g150811-d21491998-Private_Tour_Cenotes_of_Mucuyche_Santa_Barbara_in_one_day-Merida_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Both cenote personalities in one day — open + cavern","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/DMC"},{"name":"Progreso Gulf beach + Malecón + world''s-longest pier","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"The city''s ocean, 30 minutes away","bookable_category":"transfer + beach-club day","tier":"essential","source":"https://yucatan.guide/posts/progreso-beach-complete-visiting-guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"The city''s ocean, 30 minutes away","commission":"DMC/affiliate"},{"name":"Dzibilchaltún ruins + Cenote Xlacah","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Ruin + swim + museum in a half-day","bookable_category":"guided half-day","tier":"essential","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Ruin + swim + museum in a half-day","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/Viator (INAH fee pass-through)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mérida the hacienda-wedding capital, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Because the restored henequen haciendas — chapel ruins, walled gardens, private cenotes — are a wedding backdrop found nowhere else, backed by a mature, English-fluent planner ecosystem. Book the date and core vendors 6–12 months out (advisors say 10–12 for high season), the longest-lead, highest-margin flow in the destination.","source":"destinationweddings.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the best day-trips from Mérida?","a":"Cenotes and flamingos, mostly within ~1.5 hr. The closest swimmable cenote and ruin is Dzibilchaltún (~20 min); the Cuzamá/Homún cenote country is reached by horse-drawn rail-cart (~1 hr); Celestún''s flamingo biosphere is ~1.5 hr west; and Uxmal + the Ruta Puuc lie ~1.5 hr south. Chichén Itzá is ~1.5 hr east, best done at dawn.","source":"girlwiththepassport.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mérida?","a":"December through April is the dry-cool peak (highs ~84°F, lows ~64°F), but the smartest window is the late-October Hanal Pixán opening (Oct 25–Nov 2), when the heat breaks and hurricane season ends — the Festival de las Ánimas fills the streets with altars and the candlelit Paseo de las Ánimas, mostly free to attend. November and late April are softer-rate shoulders.","source":"plalla.com / traveltomerida.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What should I eat in Mérida?","a":"Yucatecan food, which stands apart from central-Mexican cooking. The signature is cochinita pibil — pork marinated in achiote and bitter orange, wrapped in banana leaves and slow-roasted in an underground pit — best at the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls), alongside sopa de lima, papadzules, salbutes and panuchos.","source":"travelyucatan.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mérida?","a":"Heat, not crime. May–September is hot-humid and April–June can exceed 100°F (38°C), so run daytime ruin and cenote-country outings on an extreme-heat protocol: dawn starts, hat and high SPF, electrolytes, a midday shade break, and no midday Chichén or Uxmal in summer. Drink bottled water only, and use repellent — dengue is present and chikungunya rose in 2025–26 (no malaria in the corridor).","source":"traveltomerida.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mérida, Yucatán Travel Guide 2026 — Haciendas, Cenotes & the White City | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Mérida, Yucatán — Mexico''s safest state (US Level 1). Luxury hacienda hotels, cenote day-trips, Chichén Itzá & Uxmal, Progreso beach, Hanal Pixán, and hacienda weddings.","slug":"merida-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mérida Yucatán travel guide","long_tail":["best time to visit Mérida Mexico","Yucatán hacienda hotels","cenotes near Mérida","Mérida hacienda wedding","Chichén Itzá day trip from Mérida","Hanal Pixán Mérida","is Mérida Mexico safe"],"search_language":"en + es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Mérida","haciendas Yucatán boda","cenotes cerca de Mérida","mejor época para visitar Mérida","Hanal Pixán Mérida","haciendas de lujo Yucatán"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"Romance & Honeymoons (RHN)","status":"live"},{"si":"Global Expedition Adventures (GEA)","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","why_ultra":"Leading Hotels of the World; 38 private-pool forest villas; sacred-cenote spa; 1,000+ bottle tequila cellar; Ixi''im destination restaurant","earning":"LHW Leaders Club / Virtuoso preferred booking — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"Upgrade on arrival, daily breakfast, spa/resort credit, early check-in / late check-out","mor":"Hotel (LHW) bills guest; TWW = advisor-of-record","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hacienda Temozón, a Luxury Collection Hotel","why_ultra":"17th-c. henequen hacienda; 28 rooms incl. owner''s-bedroom Presidential Suite; cenote spa","earning":"Marriott Luxury Collection / STARS — commission + STARS amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS: $100 property credit, room upgrade, breakfast, early/late, welcome amenity","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = STARS advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hacienda San José Cholul, a Luxury Collection Hotel","why_ultra":"15-suite henequen hacienda; open-air 19th-c. architecture; weddings to 300 guests","earning":"Marriott Luxury Collection / STARS — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity suite (credit, upgrade, breakfast, early/late)","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = STARS advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hacienda Xcanatún, Angsana Heritage Collection","why_ultra":"18th-c. sisal hacienda, 54 suites, ~25 min from Centro; Virtuoso-listed; strong weddings/honeymoons","earning":"Accor/Angsana; Virtuoso preferred — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso amenity: property credit, upgrade, breakfast, early/late","mor":"Accor bills guest; TWW = Virtuoso advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Rosas & Xocolate","why_ultra":"17-room Design Hotel boutique from two 1930s Paseo de Montejo mansions; the in-city ultra-boutique romance base","earning":"Marriott Bonvoy / Design Hotels / STARS-eligible — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS/Bonvoy amenity + upgrade","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = advisor","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Mérida, Yucatán, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.9674,"lng":-89.5926}}'::jsonb, 68),
