e house + cobblestone plazas","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate ~8% (Viator) or DMC private","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Casa Luis Barragán (UNESCO)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"the modernist master''s house-studio; tickets release Tue noon, sell out in minutes","bookable_category":"timed entry (pass-through) + architecture tour","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g150800-d184110-Reviews-Casa_Luis_Barragan-Mexico_City — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the modernist master''s house-studio; tickets release Tue noon, sell out in minutes","when":"Oct 31","commission":"concierge add-on + DMC guide","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Pujol / Quintonil tasting menus","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"top-of-the-world Mexican fine dining + taco omakase; reservations weeks out","bookable_category":"reservation/experience","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.theinfatuation.com/mexico-city/guides/best-mexico-city-restaurants — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"top-of-the-world Mexican fine dining + taco omakase; reservations weeks out","when":"Oct 31","commission":"concierge value-add (non-commissionable) — bundle into DMC ultra","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Contramar","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"the sun-drenched seafood institution; tuna tostadas + pescado a la talla","bookable_category":"reservation","tier":"premier","source":"https://joinpearl.co/restaurants/mexico-city/contramar — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"the sun-drenched seafood institution; tuna tostadas + pescado a la talla","when":"Oct 31","commission":"concierge add-on","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Mercado de San Juan","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"the gourmet market of exotic proteins + cheeses — a chef''s playground","bookable_category":"guided food tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mezcalistas.com/a-locals-guide-to-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"the gourmet market of exotic proteins + cheeses — a chef''s playground","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate ~8% or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Licorería Limantour (Roma)","si_tag":"Nightlife","status":"future","hook":"Best Bar in North America (2022 & 2023) + 2024 backroom speakeasy","bookable_category":"reservation/bar tour","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.mezcalistas.com/a-locals-guide-to-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"nightlife","blurb":"Best Bar in North America (2022 & 2023) + 2024 backroom speakeasy","when":"Oct 31","commission":"concierge add-on / guided crawl affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Mezcalerías (Templo Centro + Claraluz Coyoacán)","si_tag":"Nightlife","status":"future","hook":"2024-new prehispanic speakeasy + candlelit mezcal salon, still under the radar","bookable_category":"guided mezcal crawl","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mezcalistas.com/a-locals-guide-to-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"nightlife","blurb":"2024-new prehispanic speakeasy + candlelit mezcal salon, still under the radar","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate ~8% or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Pulquerías (Centro)","si_tag":"Nightlife","status":"future","hook":"traditional fermented-agave cantinas — a genuinely local drinking tradition","bookable_category":"guided cultural bar tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://keith.is/guides/cdmx — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"nightlife","blurb":"traditional fermented-agave cantinas — a genuinely local drinking tradition","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Lucha libre at Arena México","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"''the Cathedral'' — masked-wrestling theater in a ~17,000-seat arena","bookable_category":"guided experience + arena admission","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mexico-City/Tacos-Beer-Lucha-BEST-NIGHT-EVER/d628-86240P2 — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"''the Cathedral'' — masked-wrestling theater in a ~17,000-seat arena","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate up to ~12% (Viator) or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Día de Muertos Grand Parade","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"~6 km Nov-1 parade Chapultepec → Reforma → Zócalo; biggest live-culture moment","bookable_category":"parade-window package (hotel + guided viewing)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.casagoliana.com/blog/day-of-the-dead-parade-mexico-city-2026/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"~6 km Nov-1 parade Chapultepec → Reforma → Zócalo; biggest live-culture moment","when":"Oct 31","commission":"DMC (Fora lane) — book weeks out","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Xochimilco trajineras","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"colorful boats poled through UNESCO canals + floating gardens; mariachi afternoon","bookable_category":"private trajinera tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mexico-City/Private-Tour-in-Trajinera-through-the-Canals-of-Xochimilco/d628-289853P13 — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"colorful boats poled through UNESCO canals + floating gardens; mariachi afternoon","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate ~8% (Viator private) or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Sunday Paseo de la Reforma (Muévete en Bici)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"the grand boulevard closes to cars Sunday mornings for cyclists + walkers","bookable_category":"bike tour / self-guided","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.casagoliana.com/blog/best-time-to-visit-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"the grand boulevard closes to cars Sunday mornings for cyclists + walkers","when":"Oct 31","commission":"affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Jacaranda-season Roma-Condesa stroll + rooftop dinner","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Mar–Apr purple canopies over the prettiest neighborhoods + Polanco rooftop","bookable_category":"hotel + private guide + reservation","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.casagoliana.com/blog/best-time-to-visit-mexico-city/ — Accessed 2026-07-05","timing":"Oct 31","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Mar–Apr purple canopies over the prettiest neighborhoods + Polanco rooftop","when":"Oct 31","commission":"DMC (Fora lane)","accessed":"2026-07-05"}],"faq":[{"q":"Will the altitude affect me?","a":"It can for the first day or two. The city sits at **~2,240 m (7,349 ft)** — roughly 25% less oxygen than sea level — and most travelers need **24–72 hours** to acclimate; mild headache, fatigue and breathlessness are common on arrival from sea level and pass with rest, hydration and easing off alcohol on day one. Fitness and age do not predict susceptibility.","source":"nomadoc.com.mx, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mexico City good for a romantic city break?","a":"Strongly — it''s the one live-launch SI that genuinely fits an inland capital. The romance lane is Polanco/Reforma luxe: the St. Regis atop the **31-story Torre Libertad**, the Sofitel''s **38th-floor pool**, rooftop dining, and the March–April jacaranda bloom that turns Roma-Condesa purple.","source":"blacklane.com / casagoliana.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the must-see culture sites, and is Teotihuacán worth it?","a":"Yes — the heritage circuit runs from the Museo Nacional de Antropología (the Aztec Sun Stone) and Templo Mayor beneath the Zócalo out to Teotihuacán, ~50 km northeast, best at dawn by private balloon (**$150–$300 USD**). It''s the single greatest day-trip from the city.","source":"mexicocity-tours.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Do I need reservations for Pujol and the top restaurants?","a":"Yes — book weeks ahead. Pujol (top-5 on Latin America''s 50 Best) and Quintonil sell their tasting menus out well in advance, and Casa Luis Barragán tickets release Tuesdays at noon CDMX time and sell out within minutes. Lock the marquee tables the moment the trip is confirmed.","source":"theinfatuation.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Where''s the best nightlife and cocktail scene?","a":"Roma-Condesa. Licorería Limantour was named **Best Bar in North America in 2022 and 2023**, and the surrounding streets hold the city''s densest cluster of cocktail bars, mezcalerías and traditional pulquerías — best done as a guided crawl.","source":"mezcalistas.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"nightlife"},{"q":"When is Día de Muertos, and can I see the parade?","a":"Oct 31–Nov 2, with the Grand Parade on ~Nov 1 running **~6 km** from Chapultepec down Reforma to the Zócalo — the biggest live-culture moment of the CDMX year. Parade-corridor hotels (Centro/Reforma) tighten sharply through October, so book weeks out.","source":"casagoliana.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"entertainment"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mexico City (CDMX) Travel Guide 2026 — Culture, Food & Día de Muertos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan a Mexico City trip with TravelWell.World: when to go (Día de Muertos, jacaranda season), where to stay (Four Seasons to Roma villas), food and culture jewels, altitude and safety — all bookable.","slug":"mexico-city-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mexico City travel guide","long_tail":["best time to visit Mexico City","Día de Muertos Mexico City 2026","Mexico City altitude sickness","luxury hotels Polanco","Teotihuacán balloon day trip","Roma Condesa restaurants"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-05","search_language":"en + es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en CDMX","Día de Muertos Ciudad de México","mejores restaurantes Roma Condesa","hoteles de lujo Polanco","globo aerostático Teotihuacán","mejor época para visitar la Ciudad de México"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"nightlife","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Mexico City","why_ultra":"hacienda-style courtyard-oasis on Reforma; 240 rooms/40 suites; FS service benchmark","earning":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner / Virtuoso via host","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade + daily breakfast + $100 credit + early/late (verify)","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"St. Regis Mexico City","why_ultra":"31-story Torre Libertad; 189 rooms; butler service; best high-floor Reforma views","earning":"Marriott STARS/Luxury via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity: credit + upgrade + breakfast","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Las Alcobas (Luxury Collection, Polanco)","why_ultra":"Yabu Pushelberg 35-room jewel-box; butler; Anatol + Dulce","earning":"Marriott Luxury STARS/Luminous via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"premier-ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Mexico City Reforma","why_ultra":"French-luxe, 38th-floor pool over the city; 275+56 suites","earning":"Accor Sofitel preferred / Virtuoso via host (Fora)","virtuoso_value_add":"preferred-partner amenity","mor":"hotel/chain","tier":"premier-luxury"},{"name":"Casa Polanco","why_ultra":"restored 1930s aristocratic residence; villa-like intimacy w/ hotel service","earning":"verify Virtuoso/preferred membership at booking","virtuoso_value_add":"TBD per program","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier-ultra"},{"name":"Pug Seal boutiques (Polanco)","why_ultra":"tiny art-filled design micro-hotels for boutique-over-grand ultra travelers","earning":"verify host/preferred program","virtuoso_value_add":"TBD","mor":"hotel","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"Mexico City (CDMX), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.4326,"lng":-99.1332}}'::jsonb, 69),
  ('monteverde-costa-rica', '10S', 'Monteverde', 'Costa Rica', 'The original cloud forest', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Costa Rica', '{"expedition","wildlife","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Birthplace of the commercial canopy zipline; Selvatura runs 13 ziplines incl. a 1 km line, 15 platforms, Tarzan swing, and 8 hanging bridges (51-170 m long, 12-60 m high).","Cloud forest protects 400+ bird species (resplendent quetzal, three-wattled bellbird), 2,500+ plants incl. 500+ orchids, 100+ mammals.","Three reserves: Monteverde Cloud Forest ($25, 7AM-4PM), Santa Elena (quieter, great quetzals), Curi-Cancha (least crowded, top birding).","Resplendent quetzal breeds Feb-Jun (peak Mar-Apr), best viewed 6-9 AM on wild-avocado trees.","Highland ~1,400 m; ~3-4 hr from SJO with a rough, partly-unpaved final mountain road; dengue risk low at elevation."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_clinic":"Santa Elena local clinics (minor/first response)","major_trauma":"San Jose hospitals (CIMA, Clinica Biblica), ~3-4 hr by road; air/ground evac pathway","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_reason":"Crime (petty nationwide; some violent crime, concentrated in specific San Jose neighborhoods)","advisory_issued":"2026-04-02","standard_caution":"No valuables in parked rental cars; registered operators; daylight driving on mountain road","activity_hazards":["zipline/canopy operator certification + harness/brakes + weight limits","mountain-road fog + unpaved sections (4WD, daylight)","night-walk footing + vipers (guided only)","wet suspension-bridge decking + heights"],"book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"SJO (Juan Santamaria) ~3-4 hr road; note rough/partly-unpaved access road","water":"Tap water generally potable including Monteverde area; bottled optional for sensitive travelers","dengue":"Low at ~1,400 m highland elevation; use repellent","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}},"timing":{"national_dry_peak":"mid-December to April","holiday_hard_peak":"late December","quetzal_breeding":"February to June/July, peak March-April","green_secret_season":"May-June (low crowds, birding-rich, misty year-round)","wettest_month":"October","curve_start_dry":"early-mid December","curve_start_quetzal":"early February","fire_date":"late November (~Nov 20-27) for dry/holiday; mid-late January (~Jan 20-27) for quetzal-birding","booking_lead":"60-90 days peak; 2-4 weeks green season","note":"misty year-round; peak demand != peak experience; sharpen on live tracking"},"jewels":[{"name":"Selvatura Park canopy + bridges","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.selvatura.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","when":"year-round","commission":"Activities-Well direct or DMC bundle"},{"name":"Sky Adventures (SkyTram/SkyTrek/SkyWalk)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://eternalarrival.com/ziplining-in-monteverde-canopy-tours/","si":"expedition","commission":"Activities-Well / DMC"},{"name":"100% Aventura (Superman ziplines)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://mytanfeet.com/activities/100-aventura-monteverde/","si":"expedition","commission":"Activities-Well / DMC"},{"name":"Guided night wildlife walk","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/night-walk-monteverde/","hook":"uneven, wet, dark footing — guided only; wear grippy footwear, follow the guide''s beam, watch for vipers","si":"expedition","blurb":"uneven, wet, dark footing — guided only; wear grippy footwear, follow the guide''s beam, watch for vipers","commission":"Activities-Well / DMC"},{"name":"San Luis Waterfall","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.airbnb.com/monteverde-costa-rica/stays/villas","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC / guide"},{"name":"Monteverde Cloud Forest Reserve (quetzal)","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://monteverdetravel.com/quetzal-season-in-monteverde/","si":"wildlife","commission":"guide/DMC; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Santa Elena Reserve","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.enjoycostarica.com/blog/monteverde-cloud-forest-a-complete-guide-for-nature-lovers/","si":"wildlife","commission":"guide/DMC; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Curi-Cancha Reserve","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://mytanfeet.com/activities/birdwatching-at-curi-cancha-reserve/","si":"wildlife","commission":"guide/DMC; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Bat Jungle","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://monteverdecostarica-info.weebly.com/monteverde-bat-jungle.html","si":"wildlife","commission":"affiliate/pass-through"},{"name":"Butterfly Garden + glass-frog vivarium","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://tours.co.cr/activities-in-monteverde/","si":"wildlife","commission":"affiliate/pass-through"},{"name":"Monteverde Cheese Factory (La Lecheria) + coffee","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.costarica-spirit.com/destinations/monteverde/","si":"wildlife","commission":"DMC/guide add-on"},{"name":"Hidden Canopy Treehouses (adults-only)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.enchantingtravels.com/hotels/monteverde/hidden-canopy-treehouse/","si":"romance","commission":"consortia/DMC"}],"faq":[{"q":"Which is the best zipline in Monteverde?","a":"It depends on your appetite. Selvatura''s flagship runs 13 ziplines including a 1 km line, 15 platforms, a Tarzan swing and 8 hanging bridges; 100% Aventura is the adrenaline pick with 11 ziplines including two Superman lines; Sky Adventures is the family-friendly tram-up, zip-down option.","source":"selvatura.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is quetzal season in Monteverde?","a":"Peak sightings run February–June (breeding), with March–April the sweet spot. Best hours are 6–9 AM, when males feed on wild avocado; a guided dawn quetzal walk (~$40–80, 2–3 hrs) is among Costa Rica''s best-value wildlife experiences.","source":"monteverdetravel.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife-&-nature-—-future"},{"q":"Is Monteverde good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — it''s a genuine eco-romance hub, not a beach substitute. Adults-only Hidden Canopy Treehouses are the honeymoon centerpiece, and Hotel Belmar offers Forest Superior rooms with a jacuzzi and private terrace for a mist-and-forest soak; both run boutique-luxe, not palace-scale.","source":"enchantingtravels.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is ziplining in Monteverde dangerous?","a":"It''s high-consequence if gear or technique fails, so ride only with certified operators. Confirm harness and dual-brake systems, helmet and stated weight limits before booking with Selvatura, Sky Adventures or 100% Aventura — high-speed lines and Superman/Tarzan configurations raise the stakes.","source":"selvatura.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How hard is the drive to Monteverde?","a":"It''s a real mountain climb. Monteverde sits at ~1,400 m, roughly 3–4 hours from Juan Santamaría (SJO), with the final stretch a rough, partly-unpaved and fog-prone road — drive in daylight, 4WD recommended, allow extra time.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Monteverde Cloud Forest, Costa Rica: Quetzals, Ziplines & Cloud-Forest Lodges | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Monteverde - the original cloud-forest zipline, resplendent-quetzal birding, hanging bridges, night walks, and boutique eco-lodges. Best times, safety, and how to book.","long_tail_en":["Monteverde cloud forest guide 2026","best zipline in Monteverde","resplendent quetzal season Monteverde","Monteverde vs Santa Elena reserve","Monteverde hanging bridges","Monteverde night walk","luxury eco lodge Monteverde","how to get to Monteverde from San Jose","Monteverde honeymoon treehouse"],"search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["bosque nuboso Monteverde","canopy Monteverde","reserva Santa Elena","quetzal Monteverde temporada","puentes colgantes Monteverde","tour nocturno Monteverde","hoteles ecologicos Monteverde","como llegar a Monteverde"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister - commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","wildlife","romance"],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Belmar","type":"premier boutique eco-lodge","note":"CST level 5, first carbon-neutral in Monteverde, brewery, Nicoya Suites ~1000sqft, ~$270-1200/nt; Design Hotels + Mr&Mrs Smith listed; no confirmed Virtuoso","consortia":"Design Hotels / Mr & Mrs Smith / Fora","mor":"consortia commission or DMC block","tier":"premium-boutique (NOT ultra-palace)"},{"name":"Hidden Canopy Treehouses","type":"adults-only luxury treehouses","note":"R&H apex, secluded canopy","consortia":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"premium-boutique"},{"name":"Senda Monteverde","type":"modern sustainable boutique","note":"private trails, farm-to-table","consortia":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"premium-boutique"},{"name":"Koora Monteverde","type":"newest boutique eco-lodge","note":"26 rooms (10 suites/6 bungalows/10 forest)","consortia":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"premium-boutique"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Monteverde, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":10.301,"lng":-84.8259}}'::jsonb, 70),
  ('nosara-costa-rica', '10S', 'Nosara & the Nicoya Peninsula', 'Costa Rica', 'Sunrise vinyasa over a Blue Zone shore', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Costa Rica', '{"tropical","expedition","wellness"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Nicoya Peninsula is Costa Rica''s Blue Zone — historically ~3-4x the global centenarian rate (2013 study).","Playa Guiones (Nosara) offers consistent year-round surf — Nosara sees 300+ surfable days a year.","Ostional Wildlife Refuge (est. 1984) hosts olive-ridley arribadas of up to ~500,000 turtles, peaking Sep-Oct.","Santa Teresa / Mal Pais is the peninsula''s boho-luxury surf-and-sunset coast, remote southern tip.","LIR (Liberia) is ~2.5-3 hr drive to Nosara; Tambor (TMU) is a 25-min flight + 25-min drive to Santa Teresa."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"nearest_trauma":"Nicoya town hospital (stabilize) -> CIMA Guanacaste (Liberia) / CIMA San Jose (major) -> air evac ($20k-$100k+) for extreme trauma","advisory_reasons":["crime (petty + violent)","deadly rip currents"],"riptide":"STRONG at Playa Guiones & Santa Teresa; swim only in guarded/designated zones","activity_fires":["surf/riptides (beginner Guiones vs advanced Santa Teresa)","ATV/quad on unpaved roads (leading local injury)","turtle arribada (guided-only, no lights)","waterfall jumping (Montezuma)"],"road_remoteness_flag":"Santa Teresa/Mal Pais — unpaved sections, green-season river crossings, slow trauma response","dengue":"present, wet-season peak","water":"potable in developed towns; bottled/filtered common in remote beach communities — verify locally","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}},"timing":{"curve_start":"late-Oct to early-Nov","peak":"mid-December to April (dry season)","shoulder":"May-June & November","green":"July-October (wet; bigger surf swell; arribada peak)","surf":"year-round; green-season swells bigger (counter-seasonal draw)","arribada":"year-round, peaks Jul-Nov (biggest Sep-Oct), lunar-timed near last-quarter & new moon","retreat_booking_lead":"3-6 months","fire_date":"mid-September"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Guiones surf","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.vacationscostarica.com/nosara/","hook":"300+ day beach break; the beginner-to-intermediate teaching wave","si":"expedition","blurb":"300+ day beach break; the beginner-to-intermediate teaching wave","commission":"surf-school/retreat direct + affiliate"},{"name":"Nosara yoga core (Nosara Yoga Institute / Bodhi Tree / Harmony)","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"premier","source":"https://bodhitreeyogaresort.com/","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the genuine, lived-in yoga capital: daily classes, teacher trainings, sound baths, healing/energy work","si":"wellness","blurb":"the genuine, lived-in yoga capital: daily classes, teacher trainings, sound baths, healing/energy work","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"retreat operator + BookYogaRetreats affiliate + hotel MoR"},{"name":"Ostional arribada","si_tag":"GEA (wildlife)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.wcanosara.org/arribadas","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Year-round but peaks Jul–Nov; events cluster on the ~28-day lunar cycle","si":"GEA (wildlife)","blurb":"Year-round but peaks Jul–Nov; events cluster on the ~28-day lunar cycle","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"guided community tour + lodging MoR (refuge fee non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Santa Teresa / Mal Pais surf + boho-luxe sunset","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.vacationscostarica.com/santa-teresa/rentals/","hook":"advanced swell coast + sunset-bar culture; the peninsula''s cool jewel","si":"GEA/Romance","blurb":"advanced swell coast + sunset-bar culture; the peninsula''s cool jewel","commission":"villa/hotel MoR + DMC"},{"name":"Montezuma waterfalls + Cabo Blanco reserve","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/cabo-blanco-nature-reserve/","hook":"challenging jungle trek to a white-sand reward beach; seabird + wildlife","si":"expedition","blurb":"challenging jungle trek to a white-sand reward beach; seabird + wildlife","commission":"guided-tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Sámara calm-bay family beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.costaricarios.com/the-top-16-must-do-highlights-of-the-nicoya-peninsula/","si":"tropical","commission":"villa/hotel MoR + DMC transfer"},{"name":"Playa Barrigona (hidden)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.costaricarios.com/the-top-16-must-do-highlights-of-the-nicoya-peninsula/","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"villa MoR + guided transfer"},{"name":"Sloth / howler jungle wildlife","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thetravnav.com/the-best-nosara-costa-rica-guide-things-to-do/","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Nosara/Cabo Blanco forests hold sloths, howler monkeys, scarlet macaws — guided wildlife walks","si":"expedition","blurb":"Nosara/Cabo Blanco forests hold sloths, howler monkeys, scarlet macaws — guided wildlife walks","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"guided-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Blue Zone longevity + food","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.specialplacesofcostarica.com/blog/blue-zone-costa-rica-living-longer-living-better/","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"plant-forward Nicoyan diet, garden-to-table, longevity-lifestyle immersion; the destination''s signature intangible","si":"wellness","blurb":"plant-forward Nicoyan diet, garden-to-table, longevity-lifestyle immersion; the destination''s signature intangible","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"culinary/wellness experience + retreat packages"},{"name":"SUP the Nosara river estuary","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thetravnav.com/the-best-nosara-costa-rica-guide-things-to-do/","timing":"mid-December to April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"mangrove + birdlife paddle where the river meets Guiones; low-risk family adventure","si":"expedition","blurb":"mangrove + birdlife paddle where the river meets Guiones; low-risk family adventure","when":"mid-December to April","commission":"outfitter affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"Which Nicoya beach is best for families and calm swimming?","a":"Sámara is the pick. Its long horseshoe bay is calm and reef-protected, making it the peninsula''s safest swim and best family beach for kayaking, snorkeling and SUP — a gentler alternative to the surf breaks at Guiones and Santa Teresa.","source":"costaricarios.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Nosara good for beginner surfers?","a":"Yes — Playa Guiones is a forgiving beach break with surf schools and whitewater, and Nosara sees 300+ surfable days a year, so beginners can learn nearly any day. Advanced surfers should head to the heavier point/reef swell at Santa Teresa / Mal País instead.","source":"vacationscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the Ostional turtle arribada?","a":"Year-round, but it peaks Jul–Nov and is biggest Sep–Oct, when up to ~500,000 olive-ridleys come ashore. Events cluster on the ~28-day lunar cycle — around the last-quarter moon and the dark nights just before the new moon — and access is guided-only.","source":"volunteerlatinamerica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Nosara or Santa Teresa better for a honeymoon?","a":"Both work — pick your mood. Nosara pairs wellness-retreat honeymoons with its lived-in yoga scene; Santa Teresa / Mal País is the remote boho-luxury surf-and-sunset coast, with elite jungle-beach villas and barefoot-ultra properties like Latitude 10 for total privacy.","source":"vacationscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is the Nicoya Blue Zone?","a":"It''s Costa Rica''s official Blue Zone — one of only five global longevity zones. A 2013 study found the region had roughly 3–4× the global proportion of centenarians, and Nosara''s yoga culture is local and lived-in, not imported for tourists.","source":"specialplacesofcostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wellness-&-spa-—-future"},{"q":"What''s the #1 safety risk on this coast?","a":"Rip currents. The State Department explicitly warns that dozens of U.S. citizens die yearly in Costa Rica surf, and both Guiones and Santa Teresa have strong riptides — swim only in designated/guarded areas and heed local surf-instructor guidance.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can anyone watch the Ostional arribada?","a":"No — access is guided-only. Ostional is a community-managed refuge where guided access is mandatory, with no lights or flash and no touching, respecting nesting-window rules; unguided night beach access is both a wildlife-harm and personal-safety issue.","source":"wcanosara.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Nosara & the Nicoya Peninsula, Costa Rica — Blue Zone Yoga, Surf & Turtle Coast | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["Nosara yoga surf","Santa Teresa Costa Rica","Península de Nicoya playas","arribada Ostional","Zona Azul Nicoya longevidad","retiro de yoga Nosara"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["Tropical Islands & Beaches (LIVE)","GEA (LIVE)","Wellness & Spa (FUTURE)"],"ultra":[{"name":"Latitude 10 Exclusive Beach Resort","location":"Santa Teresa","tier":"ultra","path":"MoR + Fora/consortia amenity"},{"name":"Hotel Nantipa","location":"Santa Teresa","tier":"luxury-ultra","path":"SLH/consortia + MoR"},{"name":"The Harmony Hotel","location":"Nosara","tier":"luxury","path":"consortia + MoR"},{"name":"Bodhi Tree Yoga Resort","location":"Nosara","tier":"premier","path":"retreat operator + MoR"},{"name":"Nosara/Santa Teresa branded luxury villas","location":"Nicoya","tier":"ultra","path":"MoR"},{"name":"Nalu (Santa Teresa)","location":"Santa Teresa","tier":"luxury","path":"verify — thin sourcing"},{"name":"Origins Lodge / Kinkára","location":"VERIFY — likely NOT Nicoya","tier":"ultra","path":"excluded pending region confirmation"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Nosara & the Nicoya Peninsula, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.976,"lng":-85.653}}'::jsonb, 71)
